    """{"unit_info.action.build_menu.label":"Build","unit_info.action.reinforce_menu.label":"Reinforce","unit_info.action.reinforce.menu_label":"Veterans","unit_info.action.green_reinforce.menu_label":"Recruits","unit_info.action.actions_back.label":"Back","unit_info.action.actions_more.label":"More","unit_info.action.build_bridge.short_label":"Bridge","unit_info.action.build_fortification.short_label":"Fort","unit_info.action.build_airfield.short_label":"Airfield","unit_info.action.build_port.short_label":"Port","unit_info.action.build_station.short_label":"Station","attachments.available":"Available","attachments.close.help":"Close","attachments.cost":"{cost} pp","attachments.cost.unavailable":"unavailable","attachments.count":"{fitted} of {max} fitted","attachments.done":"Done","attachments.grant.bridging":"Grants: acts as a bridge over rivers/streams","attachments.grant.bunker_buster":"Grants: against bunkers and units on fortification hexes only, ignores their entrenchment and rugged defence","attachments.grant.fast_builder":"Builds and repairs {turns} turn(s) faster, never under 1 turn","attachments.none":"Nothing can be fitted to this formation.","attachments.open.help":"Attachments: fit up to two per formation. Each carries a bonus and a stated penalty.","attachments.penalty.none":"no penalty","attachments.total_cost":"Cost: {cost} pp","attachments.slot.empty":"empty","attachments.slot.pending":"Not bought yet \u2014 click to take it back","attachments.slot.label":"Slot {n}","attachments.stat.airdefence":"AA / Air Defence","attachments.stat.ammo":"Ammo","attachments.stat.entrenchment":"Entrenchment","attachments.stat.fuel":"Fuel","attachments.stat.hardattack":"Hard Attack","attachments.stat.initiative":"Initiative","attachments.stat.modified":"{stat} {delta} from attachments ({source})","attachments.stat.munition":"Hit roll (each point: +5% per shot)","attachments.stat.movement":"Movement","attachments.stat.observer":"Attack for friendly artillery, AD and ships firing at adjacent targets","attachments.stat.spot":"Spotting","attachments.stat.unknown":"bonus","attachments.unaffordable.help":"Not enough prestige for this attachment.","bridge.laying.alert":"Laying a crossing","bridge.laying":"{unit} is laying a crossing here \u2014 it opens next turn","bridge.ready.alert":"Crossing ready","bridge.ready":"{unit}: the crossing is ready \u2014 friendly units can pass through this hex","briefing.sides":"{left} vs {right}","briefing.sides.commanded":"{left} vs {right} \u2014 you command the {commanded}","calendar.month.short.0":"Jan","calendar.month.short.1":"Feb","calendar.month.short.10":"Nov","calendar.month.short.11":"Dec","calendar.month.short.2":"Mar","calendar.month.short.3":"Apr","calendar.month.short.4":"May","calendar.month.short.5":"Jun","calendar.month.short.6":"Jul","calendar.month.short.7":"Aug","calendar.month.short.8":"Sep","calendar.month.short.9":"Oct","calendar.year.bce":"{year} BC","campaign.back.help":"Return to the main menu without starting a campaign.","campaign.counter":{"one":"{count} campaign","other":"{count} campaigns"},"campaign.country.label":"Country","campaign.camp6bn4.title":"Greece: Resistance and Civil War (1940\u20131949)","campaign.novemberrevolution.title":"The November Revolution (1918)","campaign.rhu.title":"Hungarian Soviet Republic (1919)","campaign.camp6bn9.title":"Red Army Campaign (1936\u20131945)","campaign.camp6bn9.description":"Sese\u00f1a, October 1936: Soviet tanks go into action for the first time, on the dusty approaches to Madrid. Nine years and twenty-one battles later, the same career ends on the Manchurian frontier. In between lie Lake Khasan and Khalkhin Gol, the ice of the Raate Road, the catastrophe at Bia\u0142ystok\u2013Minsk, the winter counterblow before Moscow, the Tatsinskaya raid, Kursk, Belgrade, Balaton and the road to Vienna.\n\nThis is the Red Army's decade of apprenticeship, and every new war punishes the habits the last one taught. In Story Mode, a staff of recurring officers argues over the map before each operation, and the briefings end in hard bargains: push the timetable for prestige and hardened troops, or spend it on fuel, shells and a reserve against the counterstroke.","campaign.camp6bn5.description":"No front line. No relief column. No second chance. Your orders read like a thriller: strike the battleship Tirpitz at anchor with a commando raid. Get a stranded American politician through a captured port to a British submarine waiting offshore. Knock out two Luftwaffe airfields so that a hidden German railway gun called Bruno can finally be hunted down.\n\nTen missions take a Soviet partisan command from the rearguard fighting of 1941 through the forests of the Baltic and Belarus to the Narva breakthrough, and finally into Manchuria in August 1945. You will almost never have the numbers. Strike where the enemy feels safe, split your force when the plan demands it, and vanish before the punitive columns arrive. The title is not a slogan. It is the brief.","campaign.camp6bn8.description":"Summer 1941. The kingdom has fallen in eleven days, and in the Ma\u010dva a few hundred fighters decide the occupation will not be a quiet one. Take the Partisans from the uprising at Bela Crkva and the betrayal at U\u017eice into the great offensives meant to annihilate them: Case White on the Neretva, Case Black on the Sutjeska, and German paratroopers dropping on Tito's headquarters at Drvar.\n\nNineteen battles turn a guerrilla band into an army corps. Rail raids and hit-and-run strikes give way to Belgrade, Knin, Mostar, Sarajevo and the race for Trieste, and even after Germany surrenders, one last Axis column in Slovenia refuses to lay down its arms. The mountains made this army. Now it must come down from them and win.","campaign.reddestiny.description":"Spring 1946. In this alternate history the Western powers do not stop at plans: the British attack the Soviet forces in Germany without warning, with re-armed German divisions in their first line. The Red Army holds on the Oder, and you take command as the counteroffensive begins - clearing an armed rising at Bia\u0142ystok behind the front, then storming the Seelow Heights and Berlin itself.\n\nHow you take Berlin decides where you are sent next: to Siberia and Kazakhstan against Chiang Kai-shek's invasion, to the British bases in southern Italy, or to Greece and Crete. Every road meets again in the Low Countries, the Ardennes and at Dunkirk. A decisive blow there opens the Channel at once; anything less means Franco's Spain, Gibraltar and a Western-armed rising in the Ukraine first. At the end of both roads, London is waiting.","campaign.ncampdfn.description":"Dawn, 25 June 1950. Soviet-built tanks cross the 38th parallel, Seoul falls in days, and within weeks the Korean People's Army is hammering at the Pusan perimeter. One more push and the whole peninsula is yours. Then the enemy lands behind you, and the pursuer becomes the hunted.\n\nFourteen battles follow the war through every violent reversal: a last stand short of the Yalu, a flight behind enemy lines to lead cut-off partisans at Majon-ni, the Chinese intervention, the deep raid on Wonju and the great spring offensives of 1951. The enemy owns the sky. Every road in daylight is a gamble, and every hill is a place to hide an army.","campaign.aljf.description":"\"Lieber Freund, not much time to write...\" So begins a correspondence that will span two continents and seventeen years. Its author takes up a rifle for the German revolution of 1848, marches with Hecker's volunteers and the Palatinate insurgents, and watches the Prussian army crush every hope at Wagh\u00e4usel.\n\nExile is not the end of the story. In America, the Forty-Eighters take up arms again, this time for the Union and against slavery. Seize the St. Louis Arsenal, win Missouri, then follow the letters through Pea Ridge, Fredericksburg, Vicksburg and Gettysburg, down to Mobile Bay and on to a final assault on Richmond. Twenty-six battles, one lifelong cause: the revolution lost in Baden may yet be won in Virginia.","campaign.rhu.description":"Spring 1919. Budapest has proclaimed a Soviet republic, and the armies of its neighbours are already on the march. You are the commissar sent to the front: first to break out of the trap at Zilah, then to hold the Tisza bridgehead at Szolnok while the capital holds its breath.\n\nThen the Hungarian Red Army does the impossible. Tens of thousands of factory workers march north, Miskolc and Kassa fall, and the offensive reaches the Polish border at B\u00e1rtfa. But every triumph is borrowed time, and in July the republic stakes everything on a last throw across the Tisza. Between battles, commanders and people's commissars clash over what the revolution can afford, and your decisions shape the army that fights for its survival.","campaign.ccampdfc.description":"\"Comrade Commander! Come quickly, we must act swiftly.\" Your political commissar has arrived at Voronezh with orders from Moscow, and the Red cavalry mounts up. Ahead lies a year in the saddle: the drive on Rostov, the long ride to the Polish front, the breakthrough at Brody and the gallop towards Lw\u00f3w.\n\nThen the horsemen are caught. At Komar\u00f3w, in the last great cavalry battle, the trap closes around you; at Kakhovka and Perekop, the war against Wrangel becomes a war of wire and trenches that no charge can leap. Thirteen battles from Voronezh to Sevastopol ask one question: can you tell the moment for sabres from the moment for machine-gun carts, horse artillery and armoured trains?","campaign.novemberrevolution.description":"November 1918. The admirals order the High Seas Fleet out for one last death ride. In Kiel, the sailors refuse and elect you to lead them. Four battles carry the uprising from the naval base to Wilhelmshaven, Frankfurt and finally Berlin, where the Kaiser has ordered a J\u00e4ger regiment into a burning capital.\n\nThis is a revolution run by committee, and the committee never stops arguing. Free the prisoners or seize the telegraph? Take the town hall or the barracks? Spread the uprising or secure what you already hold? Every decision changes the forces the councils lend you. A monarchy can fall in a week, if you are the one who makes it fall.","campaign.volarm.description":"You are a former Imperial officer who has taken the Soviet oath, and for two years you will be outgunned by your own class. Denikin has British rifles, British shells, British tanks and Entente squadrons in the Black Sea. You have militia who must first be taught to dig, a railway that keeps getting cut, and orders that usually amount to holding something for four more days.\n\nNineteen operations from the Don to the Crimea. Shut the Don crossings behind the Ice March. Hold Ekaterinodar while Kornilov throws his cadets at it. Walk the Taman columns out along the coast road with the sea on one flank and the mountains on the other. Give ground across the Kuban, the Terek and the Manych as the Moscow Directive rolls north, and remember that you are judged on the task you were given, not on a front that bends somewhere else.\n\nThen Orel, where the Latvian riflemen and Primakov's Chervonny Cossacks go in at Kromy and the arrows on the map finally turn south. Kharkov. A quay at Novorossiysk, where a beaten army learns how many ships the Entente actually sent. And a year later, the Sivash mud in the dark, under a wall that was never supposed to fall.\n\nLose at Orel and the campaign does not end: it gets harder. Tula, Moscow, even Petrograd against Yudenich: each one a last line, and holding any of them hands you straight back to the pursuit.","campaign.acampdf2.description":"July 1917. You are a staff captain of the old army, attached to the Czechoslovak brigade because you speak enough Czech to be useful. At Zborov you watch volunteers storm three lines of trenches while the Russian division beside them, worn out by a war it never chose, holds a meeting on whether to fight on, and somewhere between the two, you choose your side.\n\nEleven operations and nine thousand versts of railway follow. Hold the Kiev bridges beside the legionnaires and keep Bakhmach open for their trains, then watch a thrown stove leg at Chelyabinsk turn allies into enemies in a single afternoon. Fight for Samara and the gold of Kazan, get people out of Omsk alive, and push east against Kolchak and the ataman's armoured trains. On a quay at Vladivostok in 1920, the men who once held the bridges with you are waiting for a ship home, and there is too much between you to shake hands.","campaign.polsov.description":"April 1919. Every division the Republic owns is fighting Denikin and Kolchak, so the Western Front gets a half-strength brigade, four towns on a railway and orders that begin with the word \"nevertheless\". Your war against Poland starts with too little of everything, and for most of its long months it goes backwards.\n\nDelay the advance on Wilno, hold the Berezina, sit out the Latgale winter at minus twenty-five. Then the Konarmia tears open the Polish front, and the whole army surges west towards Warsaw, straight into disaster. Bring the divisions back across the Bug, break the cavalry out of the pocket at Komar\u00f3w, and dig in on the Niemen while diplomats at Riga draw a border across the ground your battalions are standing on.","campaign.gce.description":"November 1936. Franco's columns are in the suburbs, German and Italian aircraft rule the sky, and Madrid is defended by militias who have never fought as an army. Hold the capital, then forge improvised battalions into the Ej\u00e9rcito Popular at the Jarama, Guadalajara, Brunete, Aragon and the frozen ruins of Teruel.\n\nIn July 1938 the Republic stakes everything on a night crossing of the Ebro. Win decisively and history breaks open: the offensive rolls on to Zaragoza and then across the Strait to Ceuta, back to the African shore where the rebellion began. Settle for less, and you must weather the fascist counteroffensive and a last stand on the Segre. Twelve battles, and one chance to write a different ending for Spain.","campaign.ga4.description":"Khalkhin Gol, 1939. A little-known Soviet commander gathers tanks, guns and aircraft into a single blow and destroys a Japanese army on the Mongolian steppe. His name is Georgy Zhukov, and the next six years will make it a legend. Follow his war through Moscow, Rzhev, the breaking of the Leningrad blockade, Kursk and the Korsun pocket.\n\nIn the summer of 1944, Stavka lets the Marshal choose his front for Operation Bagration: the 1st Belorussian, through Bobruisk to the Vistula, or the 2nd, through Mogilev, Minsk and Grodno. Both roads lead to Pomerania and the final storm of Berlin. Seventeen operations reward the Zhukov method: meticulous preparation, crushing concentration and the nerve to commit the reserve at exactly the right hour.","campaign.spa.description":"Capua, 73 BC. A handful of gladiators break out of their school with kitchen knives and nothing to lose. Within a year they are an army: they rout Rome's troops on the slopes of Vesuvius, sack Nola and Nuceria, and send praetor after praetor fleeing.\n\nThen, in 72 BC, the revolt splits, and you must choose. March with Crixus and the Celts to strike at Rome in its own heartland, or follow Spartacus north towards the Alps and freedom. Both roads end with Crassus and his legions walling the rebels into the south of Italy. Nineteen battles ask whether slaves can outfight the legions long enough to overturn the verdict of history.","campaign.nvc.description":"December 1964. Your fighters strike at Binh Gia, and by first light the enemy is hunting them. This is a war in which the other side owns the sky, the artillery and the roads. You own the night, the jungle and time.\n\nTwelve operations span eleven years: the siege of Plei Me and the valley of Ia Drang, clashes with South Korean troops on the coast, Khe Sanh, the Tet Offensive in Hue and Da Nang, the 1971 fight for the supply lines in Laos and the battle for Kontum. Strike, vanish, strike again, until April 1975 and the final advance on Saigon.","campaign.rcampdfr.description":"22 June 1941, on the river Prut. The first shots of the southern front are fired here, and it will be three years before Soviet troops stand on this riverbank again. In between lies the fight for the Black Sea coast: Odessa under siege, Perekop, the winter landings in Crimea, Sevastopol, and the Caucasus passes where the German drive for the oil finally breaks.\n\nTwenty-seven operations turn a retreat into the long road back. Choose where the Crimean counteroffensive of 1941 goes ashore: Kerch or Feodosiya. Hold Sukhumi and Ordzhonikidze, retake Maikop, Rostov and Novorossiysk, clear the Taman peninsula, return to Odessa and Sevastopol as liberators, and carry the offensive back across the Prut to Bucharest and Sofia.","campaign.rsoc.description":"August 1927. In Nanchang, Nationalist regiments turn their guns on their own commanders, and the Chinese Red Army is born fighting for its life. Survive the Autumn Harvest Uprising and the encirclement campaigns in the Jinggang Mountains, seize Luding Bridge on the Long March, ambush the Japanese at Pingxingguan and launch the Hundred Regiments Offensive.\n\nThe civil war is only the midpoint. Cross into Korea, where only a decisive result at Seoul reopens the road to Pusan. Then history gives way: an invasion of Taiwan under the shadow of nuclear crisis, a border war on the Amur and, in Beijing in 1955, a conspiracy against Mao himself. From a mutiny to a coup, how far will your loyalty to the revolution go?","campaign.062d.description":"November 1942. On the Chir, west of Stalingrad, Operation Uranus has torn open the Axis front, and a Soviet Guards tank corps is ordered through the gap. Its war will not stop until Berlin.\n\nTwenty operations test everything deep battle demands: meeting the panzers at Prokhorovka, racing for Kiev and Zhitomir, encircling armies in Belorussia and fighting district by district into the capital of the Reich. Prestige flows freely enough to build the formidable combined-arms corps of history: T-34s, motorised infantry, self-propelled guns, engineers and Guards. Fuel, losses and timing decide whether it reaches the finish.","campaign.camp6.description":"You are Zhukov, and the German Sixth Army has just walked into your trap at Stalingrad. Close the ring, smash the Axis front on the Don, and roll south to Rostov, Sevastopol and Odessa, then back through Kharkov and Kiev to the Oder and the last fortress of the Reich: the Reichstag.\n\nThis is where history stops and this campaign keeps going. Weeks after the victory, the Western Allies open fire in Berlin, and Moscow answers by rallying German and Italian divisions, yesterday's enemies, into a new coalition against the aggressor. Drive the Allies into the sea at Dunkirk, cross the Channel, take Windsor and London, then carry the war over the Atlantic to Florida, Savannah and, at last, Washington. Twenty-seven operations from the Volga to the Potomac.","campaign.camp6bn4.description":"October 1940. Mussolini expects Greece to fall in a fortnight. Instead, your troops throw the Italians back across the Pindus and deep into Albania. Then the Wehrmacht arrives. Choose whether to face the German onslaught with the Central or the Western Macedonia Army, make a last stand at Thermopylae, and meet the paratroopers falling on Crete. Beat them there, and there will be no evacuation.\n\nAfter El Alamein comes the decision that splits the campaign, and the country, in two. Serve the Greek government from the Alexandria mutiny to the Gothic Line in Italy, or break out of a military prison in Alexandria to join ELAS in the mountains, trading your old core for new fighters of equal experience. Both roads lead to Athens in December 1944 and into the civil war, where the same battles are fought from opposite sides of the line. Companions who share your story remember what you chose.","campaign.forward.description":"Forward: the only order that never changes. Forty-four scenarios carry your Soviet army from Khalkhin Gol and the Finnish winter into the disaster of 1941: the pockets at Minsk, Kiev and Bryansk, and the last line before Moscow.\n\nThen the war begins to branch. A brilliant victory at Tula can trap Army Group Centre and end the war in 1942; a weak one throws you into street fighting in Moscow itself. After Kharkov, choose which German army group to hunt to the end: north to Leningrad, Riga and Courland; south through the Kuban, Romania and Hungary to Prague; or through the centre to the Oder, where the result at K\u00fcstrin decides between Berlin and a new war against the Western Allies, with German divisions fighting beside you or against you. Two of the three roads end in Manchuria.","campaign.simpob.description":"You are a Red commander on the Eastern Front, and for the first year of it you will be defending things you have been told cannot be held. The Czechoslovak corps has taken the Volga bridge on its way home, a committee of Constituent Assembly deputies is governing Russia out of Samara, and behind them come Kolchak, the Siberian Cossacks and six thousand versts of railway.\n\nTwenty-three operations from the Volga to Irkutsk. Hold Kazan with six hundred million roubles of Imperial gold in the vaults beneath it and a Fifth Army that has barely been formed. Survive a Urals winter at thirty below at Ufa, Khanzhin's spring offensive coming out of the thaw, and Dutov's Cossacks around Orenburg.\n\nThen Frunze turns the front around, and for a year the arrows on the map run east. Chapayev's division crosses the Belaya on rafts at Ufa. Ekaterinburg, and the Urals factories back in Soviet hands. Chelyabinsk, held at both shoulders at once. The Tobol, where the enemy's last offensive runs out of everything. And after Omsk, the Great Siberian Ice March coming down a single railway, until it ends at Irkutsk, with the Supreme Ruler in a prison cell and the remains of the gold reserve in the same town.\n\nA bad result at Chistopol does not end the campaign. It opens an emergency line of defences back towards Moscow: Kazan, Samara, Vyatka, Saratov, Ryazan, Klin. Hold any one of them and you return at once to the counteroffensive. The title is the enemy's own motto, taken from his banner.","campaign.difficulty.full.description":"Full difficulty \u2014 no starting bonuses, standard turn limit and score.","campaign.difficulty.historical.label":"Historical","campaign.difficulty.modifiers.summary":"+{startPct}% starting prestige, +{turnPct}% prestige per turn, +{turnsPct}% extra turns, -{scorePct}% score","campaign.difficulty.operational.label":"Operational","campaign.difficulty.tactical.label":"Tactical","campaign.filter.placeholder":"Filter campaigns\u2026","campaign.flow.help":"Show how scenario outcomes branch through this campaign.","campaign.operations.label":"Operations","campaign.path.help":"Expand or collapse the scenario route and its outcome-dependent branches.","campaign.path.label":"Campaign path","campaign.map.title":"Operations map \u2014 {campaign}","campaign.map.open.label":"Open operations map","campaign.map.open.help":"Show every operation of this campaign and where each result leads.","campaign.map.close.label":"Close","campaign.map.zoom_in.label":"Zoom in (+)","campaign.map.zoom_out.label":"Zoom out (\u2212)","campaign.map.fit.label":"Fit to screen (0)","campaign.map.legend.label":"Legend","campaign.map.loading":"Loading the campaign route\u2026","campaign.map.error":"This campaign's route could not be loaded.","campaign.map.hint":"Drag to move the map; the mouse wheel or a pinch zooms. Select an operation to see where each result leads.","campaign.map.stats.length":{"one":"{range} operation per playthrough","other":"{range} operations per playthrough"},"campaign.map.stats.forks":{"one":"{count} branch point","other":"{count} branch points"},"campaign.map.stats.finales":{"one":"{count} ending","other":"{count} endings"},"campaign.map.stats.linear":"no branches","campaign.map.grade.brilliant":"\u2605 Brilliant","campaign.map.grade.victory":"Victory","campaign.map.grade.tactical":"Tactical","campaign.map.grade.lose":"Defeat","campaign.map.finale.label":"Ending","campaign.map.finale.title":"Campaign ending","campaign.map.node.here":"You are here","campaign.map.legend.title":"How to read the map","campaign.map.legend.back":"Legend","campaign.map.legend.main":"Any victory","campaign.map.legend.lose":"Defeat \u2014 the campaign goes on","campaign.map.legend.choice":"Your choice in the briefing","campaign.map.legend.defeat_end":"A defeat here ends the campaign","campaign.map.legend.return":"A result here leads back to an earlier operation","campaign.map.legend.finale":"Campaign ending","campaign.map.legend.played":"Played in your campaign","campaign.map.legend.current":"Your current operation","campaign.map.detail.outcomes":"Results","campaign.map.detail.choices":"Choice in the briefing","campaign.map.detail.choice_note":"You choose in the briefing before the battle. The choice decides where any victory leads; a defeat follows its own route.","campaign.map.detail.conditional_choice":"Offered only under certain conditions.","campaign.map.detail.by_choice":"your choice","campaign.map.detail.end_victory":"the campaign ends","campaign.map.detail.end_defeat":"the campaign is lost","campaign.map.detail.prestige":"+{amount} prestige","campaign.map.detail.played":"Played: {outcome}","campaign.map.detail.finale_from":"Campaign ending after {scenario}","campaign.map.detail.finale_reached":"Your campaign ended here.","campaign.map.detail.finale_grades":"Reached with: {outcomes}.","campaign.map.outline.forks":"Branch points","campaign.map.outline.defeats":"Defeats the campaign survives","campaign.progress.full":"In progress \u00b7 operation {current}/{total}","campaign.progress.help":"Your saved progress in this campaign","campaign.progress.short":"In progress \u00b7 operation {current}","campaign.resume.label":"Resume Campaign","campaign.resume.help":"Continue the selected campaign from its saved progress.","campaign.progress.completed":"Completed","campaign.progress.defeated":"Ended in defeat","campaign.progress.last_played":"last played {when}","campaign.replace_run.confirm.title":"Start {campaign} over?","campaign.replace_run.confirm.body":"You already have {progress} in this campaign.<br>Starting over permanently replaces that saved progress.","campaign.replace_run.confirm.confirm_button":"Start Over","campaign.replace_run.start_over.label":"Start over","campaign.replace_run.start_over.help":"Discard this campaign's saved progress and start it from the beginning.","campaign.replace_archive.confirm.title":"Start {campaign} over?","campaign.replace_archive.confirm.body":"This campaign has an archived career of {count} commander(s) in the Hero Desk.<br>Starting over permanently replaces that roster and its service history.","campaign.replace_archive.confirm.confirm_button":"Start Over","campaign.replace_run.confirm.archive":"It also replaces the archived career of {count} commander(s) in the Hero Desk.","campaign.run_export.label":"Export campaign","campaign.run_export.help":"Download the selected campaign's saved run as a file, recovery copy included.","campaign.run_export.unavailable":"This campaign has no saved run in this browser to export.","campaign.run_export.done":"Campaign run exported.","campaign.run_export.failed":"This campaign's saved run could not be read.","campaign.run_import.label":"Import campaign","campaign.run_import.help":"Replace one campaign's saved run from a campaign file exported earlier. No other campaign is touched.","campaign.run_import.success":"Imported the saved run for {campaign}.","campaign.run_import.operation":"Operation {index}","campaign.run_import.scenario_turns":"{scenario}, turn {turn}/{total}","campaign.run_import.scenario_turn":"{scenario}, turn {turn}","campaign.run_import.confirm.title":"Import the saved run for {campaign}?","campaign.run_import.confirm.incoming":"This file contains:","campaign.run_import.confirm.replaces":"It permanently replaces your current run in this campaign:","campaign.run_import.confirm.replaces_nothing":"You have no run in this campaign yet, so nothing is replaced.","campaign.run_import.confirm.scope":"Only this campaign changes. Other campaigns, your named rulesets and archived Hero Desk careers are left exactly as they are.","campaign.run_import.confirm.confirm_button":"Import Campaign","campaign.run_import.error.unreadable":"That file is not a readable campaign export.","campaign.run_import.error.profile_file":"That is a full profile backup. Use Import All Campaigns on the Load Game screen.","campaign.run_import.error.write":"The imported campaign run could not be saved.","combat.counter_battery.damaged":"{gun} answers {plane} with counterbattery fire - {losses} lost","combat.counter_battery.destroyed":"{gun} destroys {plane} with counterbattery fire","combat.counter_battery.title":"Counterbattery fire","trigger.alert":"Achievement","trigger.fired":"{unit} secures a gain here","trigger.fired.prestige":"{unit} secures +{amount} prestige","trigger.reward.prestige":" (+{amount} prestige)","victory.withdrawn":"{unit} withdrew from the map ({count} of {total})","victory.withdrawn.alert":"Withdrawn","combat.misdrop.alert":"Misdrop!","combat.misdrop.scattered":"{unit} was dropped off target ({chance}% landing chance) and came down on a neighbouring hex","combat.misdrop.enemy":"{unit} was dropped off target ({chance}% landing chance) onto a hidden enemy","combat.misdrop.drifted":"{unit} drifted far off target ({chance}% landing chance) \u2014 {losses} strength lost","combat.misdrop.lost":"{unit} was dropped off target ({chance}% landing chance) with no land in reach and was lost","combat.minefield.alert":"Minefield!","combat.minefield.hidden":"{unit} walked into an undetected minefield \u2014 {losses} strength lost","combat.minefield.hidden.nodamage":"{unit} walked into an undetected minefield","combat.minefield.known":"{unit} stopped at a known minefield","combat.alert.surrendered":"Surrendered","combat.alert.captured":"Captured","combat.alert.surprised":"Surprised","combat.alert.overrun":"Overrun","combat.alert.rugged_defense":"Rugged Defense","combat.alert.attack_stopped":"Attack Stopped","combat.alert.evaded":"Evaded","combat.alert.sabotaged":"Sabotaged","combat.alert.critical_hit":"Critical Hit","combat.alert.exploit":"Exploit","unit_info.action.undo.multiplayer":"Moves cannot be undone in a multiplayer room","combat.alert.leader_gained":"New Leader","combat.alert.retreated":"Retreat","combat.alert.contact":"Enemy Contact","hud.transport_pools.air.help":"Air transport pool: {free} of {size} free.\nThe scenario author sets how many transport aircraft your side may have in use at once. An aircraft is taken when a unit embarks (from an airfield) and returns to the pool once that unit has landed.","hud.transport_pools.air.label":"Air","hud.transport_pools.naval.help":"Naval transport pool: {free} of {size} free.\nThe scenario author sets how many transport ships your side may have in use at once. A ship is taken when a unit embarks (in a port) and returns to the pool once that unit is ashore.","hud.transport_pools.naval.label":"Sea","hud.transport_pools.none.help":"This scenario grants your side no air, naval or rail transports, so no unit can embark on one. Units with their own organic transport (trucks, halftracks) still mount it as usual.","hud.transport_pools.none.label":"No transport pools","hud.transport_pools.rail.help":"Rail transport pool: {free} of {size} free.\nThe scenario author sets how many trains your side may have in use at once. A train is taken when a unit boards at a station and returns to the pool once that unit steps off.","hud.transport_pools.rail.label":"Rail","hud.log.contact":"{unit} halted on contact with an unseen enemy","hud.log.retreated":"{unit} was forced to retreat","hud.log.leader_gained":"{unit} gained a leader: {trait}","hud.log.combat.attacked":"{attacker} attacked {defender}:","hud.log.combat.inflicted":"inflicted {losses}","hud.log.combat.inflicted_destroyed":"inflicted {losses} \u2014 {defender} destroyed","hud.log.combat.lost_remaining":"lost {losses} ({remaining} remain)","hud.log.combat.lost_destroyed":"lost {losses} \u2014 unit destroyed","hud.log.combat.experience":"\u00b7 +{value} XP","hud.log.combat.note.attack_stopped":"\u00b7 support fire stopped the attack before it went in","hud.log.combat.note.evaded":"\u00b7 {defender} evaded and pulled back","hud.log.combat.note.sabotaged":"\u00b7 saboteurs disrupted {defender}, no exchange took place","hud.log.combat.note.critical_hit":"\u00b7 {defender} sunk by a critical hit","hud.log.combat.note.attacker_critical_hit":"\u00b7 {attacker} sunk by a critical hit from return fire","hud.log.combat.note.exploit":"\u00b7 {attacker} may keep moving (Exploit Success)","hud.log.surrendered":"{unit} surrendered \u2014 encircled, no retreat","hud.log.captured":"{unit} captured {place}","equipment.buy_blocked.cant_buy":"This equipment cannot be bought \u2014 it reaches the field only as a scenario unit or a reinforcement.","rules.air_fuel.help":"Off (the default): an aircraft with no fuel simply cannot take off, and stays where it is. On: flying at all costs a minimum of one third of the aircraft's full movement in fuel, however short the hop, and an aircraft that ends its turn out of fuel with no airfield or friendly carrier on or beside its hex crashes and is lost. The move overlay already accounts for the sortie minimum, so a route you can plan is a route the aircraft can finish, and every crash is listed in the turn report.","rules.air_fuel.label":"Aircraft fuel model","rules.air_fuel.value.0":"Out of fuel, an aircraft cannot take off","rules.air_fuel.value.1":"Minimum fuel per sortie; out of fuel away from base, an aircraft is lost","rules.air_zoc.help":"Air units usually have no zone of control - this is the exception, and each scenario decides for itself. With this on, a scenario that sets the option lets its aircraft project a zone of control like any ground formation. 79 of the 457 scenarios whose source can be read set it.","rules.air_zoc.label":"Aircraft extend zones of control","rules.build_and_repair.help":"Engineers with the Sapper ability build bridges, fortifications, airfields and ports for prestige over several turns, and repair what was destroyed; units able to demolish blow bridges and raze terrain outright. Off: terrain is fixed for the whole scenario.","rules.build_and_repair.label":"Build and repair","rules.barrage.help":"A formation whose equipment can bombard may shell a hex within its gun range, and an aircraft bombs the hex beneath it. A successful barrage takes strength, ammunition, fuel and two levels of entrenchment off anything hidden there, and reduces a city, airfield, port or bridge to wreckage that costs more to cross until engineers repair it. What may be wrecked is the equipment file's decision, exactly as it is for demolition charges. The shot is spent whether or not it lands, and the scenario's author must allow it.","rules.barrage.label":"Barrage fire","rules.barrage.value.0":"Off - fire is only ever aimed at something you can see","rules.barrage.value.1":"Blind fire at hexes nobody can see","rules.barrage.value.2":"Blind fire, and aimed shelling of empty hexes you can see","rules.rail_demolition.label":"Railway demolition","rules.rail_demolition.help":"Demolition units tear up the track they are standing on, and a barrage that lands on a railway cuts the line. A cut line stops armoured trains and breaks any rail-transport route through the hex; a station on it is destroyed with the rails and must be rebuilt. Sappers relay the track with Repair. Off: railways are part of the map and nothing in the battle can touch them, which is Open General's own behaviour.","rules.campaign_auto_refit.label":"Free refit between campaign battles","rules.campaign_auto_refit.help":"Open General's campaign auto-refit. When a campaign moves to its next battle, every surviving core unit is brought back to full strength with full ammo and fuel, at no prestige cost - except in the battles the campaign's author marked as having no auto-refit, where you pay for replacements in the reserve as usual. Off, all refitting between battles is paid. While this is on, losses matter less from one battle to the next, and a dialogue reward that promises a full resupply adds nothing to an army that has already been refitted. It also stays paid before a battle whose story lets you choose a resupply, so that choice keeps its value. Campaigns only; a standalone battle is unaffected.","rules.campaign_start_prestige.label":"Starting prestige set by the campaign","rules.campaign_start_prestige.help":"Open General's per-battle starting prestige. Where a campaign's author set how much prestige the enemy starts a battle with, the enemy receives it on top of its first turn's income and can spend it on new units; where the author set a starting sum for you, you receive it on top of what you carried from the last battle. Off, neither is paid, as before. Campaigns only; the Red-side reworks of the Russian Civil War campaigns carry no such budgets and are unaffected.","rules.campaign_prestige_cap.label":"Campaign prestige cap","rules.campaign_prestige_cap.help":"Open General's prestige cap. At the end of a campaign battle, the prestige award is cut to what still fits under that battle's cap once the value of the units you bought and the prestige you hold are counted. Units the campaign gave you, prototypes and overstrength do not count, and an upgraded unit counts at its new equipment's price. Off, you always receive the full award. Campaigns only; a battle without an authored cap is unaffected.","rules.carrier_deploy.help":"An aircraft whose equipment allows it may be placed onto a friendly aircraft carrier when deploying, which is otherwise impossible because a ship at sea is never in a deployment zone. Purely additive - no hex you could already deploy onto stops being one.","rules.carrier_deploy.label":"Deploy onto carriers","rules.craters.help":"A barrage that lands on open ground with nothing to wreck digs shell craters. A crater costs one extra movement point to enter, and it gives whoever holds it a floor of one entrenchment level - cover nobody had to dig. It is a floor and never a bonus, so it can never beat entrenching and shelling your own line buys you nothing. Only a barrage digs craters, so this changes nothing while barrage fire is off. Off: shells that hit open ground leave it as it was.","rules.craters.label":"Shell craters","rules.regional_supply.label":"Regional supply","rules.regional_supply.help":"OSADA's own logistics rule. Ammunition and fuel for ground units must come from a friendly city, port or railway station along a route a supply column could use: roads and railways carry it cheaply, forests, hills, swamps and mountains slow it, and the sea, impassable rivers and escarpments stop it. A known enemy closes its own hex and makes the hexes around it dearer, so a raid forces a detour and an encirclement cuts the route. Close to a source the refill is unchanged; further away it shrinks, down to a 20% emergency minimum. The unit card shows the route's share. Replacements, aircraft, ships and depots keep their own rules. Off: supply depends only on the unit's own hex and adjacent enemies.","rules.counterbattery.help":"Artillery with the Counterbattery ability answers enemy artillery that fires on one of your formations, once per turn. The reply is one-sided - the artillery being answered does not shoot back - and it spends the answering battery's own shot for the turn. Off: artillery is only ever answered by the unit it attacked.","rules.counterbattery.label":"Counterbattery fire","rules.dry_unit_penalties.help":"A unit out of ammunition defends with halved strength and halved initiative; one out of fuel has its initiative halved. An empty unit already cannot attack and a dry one cannot move - this adds the penalties on top of those prohibitions.","rules.dry_unit_penalties.label":"Empty units fight worse","rules.equipment_toggles.help":"Off (the default): a unit's class decides whether it gets reconnaissance movement and the overrun charge. On: its own equipment record decides, which can switch either on for a unit whose class would not have it, or off for one whose class would. Turning it on changes what thousands of records can do, so it is not a cosmetic setting.","rules.equipment_toggles.label":"Abilities from the record","rules.equipment_toggles.value.0":"Decided by class","rules.equipment_toggles.value.1":"Decided by the record","rules.extended_los.help":"Extended sight rules. Mountains, hills, forest, city and bocage block sight and ranged fire past them. Troops in forest are seen by enemy ground units only from an adjacent hex, and troops in forest or city are seen from the air only within two hexes. Off: sight and fire reach anything inside range regardless of what lies between.","rules.extended_los.label":"Extended line of sight","rules.extended_naval.help":"Four naval rules under one switch, because they work as one: ships return fire against artillery and forts; ships can only attack submarines from an adjacent hex; destroyers escort naval transports against submarine attacks the way fighters escort bombers; and a submarine needs a clear line of fire to attack. Two of the four take shots away - most shipped warships have a gun range above one and lose every long shot at a submarine - so this is off unless you ask for it. 238 of the 457 scenarios whose source can be read do ask for it.","rules.extended_naval.label":"Extended naval rules","rules.ground_auto_supply.help":"Off (the default): a ground formation that does nothing for a whole turn resupplies only in a city. On: it resupplies wherever it stands. Relaxing it is a balance decision, not a correction: it hands every idle formation in the field a free full refit. Enemies next to the formation block resupply either way, because a unit being shot at is not idle.","rules.ground_auto_supply.label":"Idle ground units resupply anywhere","rules.ground_auto_supply.value.0":"Only in a city","rules.ground_auto_supply.value.1":"Anywhere it stands","rules.heavy_move_fire.help":"Off (the default): a gun may move and fire in either order. On: artillery and air-defence guns have to shoot before moving, because they must be unlimbered to fire \u2014 equipment carrying the Mechanized attribute is exempt, and so is a formation with a Mechanized Veteran commander. Turning it on changes how every artillery battery is played.","rules.heavy_move_fire.label":"Guns must fire before they move","rules.heavy_move_fire.value.0":"Either order","rules.heavy_move_fire.value.1":"Fire first, unless mechanized","rules.initiative_model.help":"On (the default): who reacts first is decided by the equipment's own initiative, its attachments, the terrain the defender stands in, the crews' experience \u2014 one point per completed experience bar \u2014 and a small random swing for the uncertainty of battle, which changes what a First Strike commander is worth. The swing is rolled only when the attack is actually made, so the battle forecast is an estimate rather than an exact figure; both players in a network game roll the same swing. Off: equipment, attachments and terrain only, so the same attack always resolves the same way and the forecast is exact.","rules.initiative_model.label":"Combat initiative","rules.initiative_model.value.0":"Equipment and terrain","rules.initiative_model.value.1":"Equipment, terrain, experience and chance","rules.installation_spotting.help":"A city, port or airfield you own sees its own hex and the ones next to it even with no unit in the garrison. Off: only units see. Vision follows ownership, so a town changing hands changes who can see from it in the same turn.","rules.installation_spotting.label":"Cities and airfields watch","rules.minefields.help":"Land minefields: fields the scenario author placed, plus fields laid during play by units able to drop mines and cleared by units able to remove them. Entering a minefield you have detected costs the rest of your movement; entering one you have not also costs strength. A unit standing in a minefield has one movement point and reduced defence. Off: no minefield exists, nothing has to be laid or cleared, and any field a scenario authored is ignored.","rules.minefields.label":"Minefields","rules.naval_critical_hits.help":"A naval shot can sink its target outright. The chance rises with the firing unit's naval attack, experience and strength, falls with the target's defence and strength, is capped at 75%, and submarines add 10% whenever they are the ones firing. The equipment file supplies the multiplier - eqp-lxf sets it to 2, and it has never been applied until now. Off unless you ask for it: it sinks ships regardless of how much strength they have left.","rules.naval_critical_hits.label":"Naval critical hits","rules.provenance.scenario_authored":"Chosen by this scenario's own settings","rules.carrier_hangars.help":"Carriers and airbases hold aircraft INSIDE their hangar rather than parked beside them - out of sight, out of reach, and out of the way of the hex's one air slot. Each holds as many as its own record allows; an aircraft cannot take off again on the turn it landed; whatever is inside is refuelled and rearmed every round and goes down with its carrier or airbase. Land formations enter bunkers, landing ships and the like only where the equipment file allows it.","rules.carrier_hangars.label":"Carrier hangars","rules.green_replacements.help":"Reinforce offers a choice: veterans keep the formation's experience at the full price, recruits cost a fraction of it and dilute the experience. Prices come from the equipment file; where it sets none, Open General's defaults apply (veterans 100%, recruits 25%). Under some equipment files a commander leaves when his formation loses its last experience bar to recruits. Off: one Reinforce at the full price, which dilutes experience if \"Replacements dilute experience\" is on.","rules.green_replacements.label":"Veterans or recruits","rules.replacement_experience.label":"Replacements dilute experience","rules.replacement_experience.help":"On (the default): fresh replacements arrive untrained, so a formation's experience becomes the strength-weighted average of its veterans and its new intake \u2014 a formation at strength 3 with 400 experience rebuilt to 10 keeps 120. Combat reads whole experience bars of 100, so a small top-up may cost nothing in effect. Off: replacements never reduce experience. Overstrength is never diluted either way, and a commander's own experience is separate and never touched.","rules.replacement_experience.value.0":"Preserved","rules.replacement_experience.value.1":"Diluted","rules.snow_fuel.help":"Off (the default): a unit spends one point of fuel per movement point wherever it goes. On: two points per movement point in snow. The move overlay already accounts for it, so a route you can plan is a route the unit can finish.","rules.snow_fuel.label":"Snow doubles fuel use","rules.snow_fuel.value.0":"One fuel per movement point","rules.snow_fuel.value.1":"Two fuel per movement point in snow","rules.spotting_memory.help":"Off (the default): visibility follows your units hex by hex. On: a hex your side has seen this turn stays visible until your turn ends, so a reconnaissance element can find a target and drive on without the target disappearing again. The memory is dropped when your turn ends, so it never shows you where the enemy moved on their own turn.","rules.spotting_memory.label":"Spotted hexes stay spotted","rules.spotting_memory.value.0":"Visibility follows your units","rules.spotting_memory.value.1":"Held until your turn ends","rules.support_fire_range_falloff.help":"Off (the default): every eligible supporter fires at full strength. On: only a unit adjacent to the one being attacked supports at full strength, and anything further away supports at half. Distance is measured to the unit under attack, not to the attacker, so a battery in depth supports at half however close the assault gets to its own hex.","rules.support_fire_range_falloff.label":"Distant supporting fire is halved","rules.support_fire_range_falloff.value.0":"Always full strength","rules.support_fire_range_falloff.value.1":"Half unless adjacent to the defender","turn_report.attrition.lost":"{unit} was lost","turn_report.attrition.reason.out_of_fuel":"Out of fuel with no airfield in reach","turn_report.attrition.reason.unknown":"Lost between turns","turn_report.group.attrition":"Lost outside combat","unit_info.action.build.started":{"one":"Work begun - {count} of your turns: finishes at the end of this one","other":"Work begun - {count} of your turns, this one included"},"unit_info.action.build_airfield.help":"Lay out a field airfield, a dirt strip, on this clear hex, so aircraft can base and resupply here. Not every aircraft can use it: jets, heavy bombers and others marked \"Cannot use dirt airfields\" cannot refuel or rearm on a field airfield. A friendly Airbase unit on or beside the strip services every aircraft. Cost, duration and when work may begin are listed below, from the rules in force.","unit_info.action.build_airfield.label":"Build field airfield","unit_info.action.build_bridge.help":"Throw a bridge across this river or stream. Cost, duration and when work may begin are listed below, from the rules in force.","unit_info.action.build_bridge.label":"Build bridge","unit_info.action.build_fortification.help":"Dig a fortification on this hex. Cost, duration and when work may begin are listed below, from the rules in force.","unit_info.action.build_fortification.label":"Build fortification","unit_info.action.build_station.help":"Build a railway station on this stretch of track, so formations can board and leave a train here. Cost, duration and when work may begin are listed below, from the rules in force.","unit_info.action.build_station.label":"Build station","unit_info.action.blow_rail.label":"Cut railway","unit_info.action.blow_rail.help":"Cut the railway line under this formation. An armoured train can no longer pass through the hex and no rail transport can be routed through it, until engineers relay the track with Repair. A station here is destroyed with the rails and has to be built again. Immediate and free, but it spends the formation's whole turn; when it may be ordered is listed below.","unit_info.action.build_port.help":"Build a port on this coastal hex, so ships can resupply and troops can embark here. Cost, duration and when work may begin are listed below, from the rules in force.","unit_info.action.build_port.label":"Build port","unit_info.action.clear_mines.done":"Minefield cleared","unit_info.action.clear_mines.failed":"The clearing attempt failed \u2014 the formation is suppressed","unit_info.action.clear_mines.help":"Try to clear the minefield this formation is standing in. The attempt can fail; a failed attempt suppresses the formation. Either way it spends the turn.","unit_info.action.clear_mines.label":"Clear mines","unit_info.action.demolish.done":"Demolished","unit_info.action.demolish.help":"Blow the bridge under this formation, or raze the terrain feature it is standing on. Rails on a demolished bridge go down with it. Immediate and free, but it spends the formation's whole turn; when it may be ordered is listed below.","unit_info.action.demolish.label":"Demolish","unit_info.action.effect.build_turns":{"one":"{amount} of your turns: finishes at the end of this one","other":"{amount} of your turns, this one included"},"unit_info.action.effect.clear_minefield":"{amount}% chance to clear the minefield","unit_info.action.effect.clear_minefield_risk":"A failed attempt suppresses the formation","unit_info.action.effect.demolish_now":"Destroys it at once","unit_info.action.effect.experience_dilution":"Experience {detail} \u2192 {amount}, diluted by untrained replacements","campaign.row.operations":{"one":"{count} operation","other":"{count} operations"},"campaign.select.help":"Choose the campaign whose briefing, nation, length and starting prestige are shown.","campaign.selection.title":"Campaign Selection","campaign.start.help":"Start the selected campaign at the chosen difficulty.","campaign.start.label":"Start Campaign","campaign.start_prestige.label":"Start prestige","combat.enemy.chip.entrenchment.bypassed.help":"Entrenchment \u2014 your selected unit ignores it","combat.enemy.chip.entrenchment.help":"Entrenchment","combat.enemy.chip.entrenchment_bypassed":"ENT BYPASSED","combat.enemy.chip.entrenchment_bypassed.help":"Your selected unit ignores this defender's entrenchment entirely, so the value shown does not apply to your attack.","combat.enemy.chip.experience.help":"Enemy formation experience","combat.enemy.chip.initiative_cap":"INI CAP {cap}","combat.enemy.chip.initiative_cap.help":"Initiative capped at {cap} by terrain (base {base})","combat.enemy.chip.mounted.help":"Mounted in organic transport","combat.enemy.chip.suppression.help":"Temporary suppression","combat.enemy.chip.support.help":"Combat Support is active","combat.enemy.chip.surprised.help":"Surprise penalties are active","combat.enemy.class.unknown":"Unit","combat.enemy.commander.fallback":"Commander","combat.enemy.factors.entrenchment":"Entrenchment: {value}","combat.enemy.factors.entrenchment_bypassed":"Entrenchment is bypassed by your selected unit","combat.enemy.factors.experience":"Experience: {value}","combat.enemy.factors.hidden_supply":"Exact ammo and fuel remain hidden by current spotting rules.","combat.enemy.factors.initiative_cap":"Initiative capped at {cap} by terrain (base {base})","combat.enemy.factors.leader":"Leader: {name}","combat.enemy.factors.mounted":"Mounted state is active","combat.enemy.factors.suppression":"Suppression: {value}","combat.enemy.factors.support":"Combat Support: +{value} effective experience bar(s)","combat.enemy.factors.surprised":"Surprise state is active","combat.enemy.factors.terrain":"Terrain: {terrain}","combat.enemy.factors.title":"Combat factors","combat.enemy.side_country_layer":"{country} \u00b7 {layer}","combat.enemy.stat":"STR {strength}/10 \u00b7 EXP {experience} \u00b7 ENT {entrenchment} \u00b7 DEF {ground} ground / {air} air","combat.enemy.sub":"{class} \u00b7 {country} \u00b7 {terrain}","combat.enemy.terrain.unknown":"Unknown terrain","combat.interception.damaged":"{gun} intercepted {plane} \u2014 {losses} strength lost","combat.interception.destroyed":"{gun} intercepted and destroyed {plane}","combat.interception.title":"Anti-aircraft interception","combat.layer.air":"air layer","combat.layer.ground":"ground layer","common.back.label":"Back","common.cancel.label":"Cancel","common.close.label":"Close","common.close_esc.help":"Close (Esc)","common.none":"None","common.unknown":"Unknown","controls.close.label":"Close","controls.command.air_mode.help":"Switch the active map layer between ground/naval and aircraft. It decides which unit a click on a stacked hex targets.","controls.command.air_mode.label":"Air Mode","controls.command.artillery_range.help":"Hatch the hexes your own artillery covers in red and the hexes spotted enemy artillery covers in black.","controls.command.artillery_range.label":"Artillery range","controls.command.close.help":"Close the topmost window. With nothing open, it opens the pause menu.","controls.command.close.label":"Close / Pause","controls.command.embark.help":"Load the selected unit onto air or naval transport at a suitable facility, or unload it.","controls.command.embark.label":"Embark / Disembark","controls.command.equipment.help":"Open or close the buy, upgrade and reserve window.","controls.command.equipment.label":"Equipment","controls.command.help.help":"Open or close this card.","controls.command.help.label":"Controls","controls.command.hex_grid.help":"Show or hide the hex outlines.","controls.command.hex_grid.label":"Hex grid","controls.command.inspector.help":"Pin or unpin the selected unit's statistics panel.","controls.command.inspector.label":"Unit inspector","controls.command.map_labels.help":"Show or hide the name labels on optional capture points. Victory objectives stay labelled either way.","controls.command.map_labels.label":"Optional objective labels","controls.command.mount.help":"Board or leave the selected unit's own transport. It does not grant a second move.","controls.command.mount.label":"Mount / Dismount","controls.command.next_unit.help":"Select the next unit that can still act this turn.","controls.command.next_unit.label":"Next unit","controls.command.overstrength.help":"Raise a full-strength veteran above 10 points, up to the ceiling its experience allows.","controls.command.overstrength.label":"Overstrength","controls.command.pan.help":"Scroll the map view. Holding a key keeps scrolling.","controls.command.pan.label":"Pan map","controls.command.prev_unit.help":"Select the previous unit that can still act this turn.","controls.command.prev_unit.label":"Previous unit","controls.command.reinforce.help":"Buy strength points back up to full for the selected unit.","controls.command.reinforce.label":"Reinforce","controls.command.reserves.help":"Open the same window directly on its Reserve tab, for deployment.","controls.command.reserves.label":"Reserves","controls.command.strategic_map.help":"Zoom out to the whole-map overview and back.","controls.command.strategic_map.label":"Strategic map","controls.command.supply.help":"Restore ammunition and fuel. The amount depends on the hex's supply factors.","controls.command.supply.label":"Supply","controls.command.turn_report.help":"Open or close the turn report with this turn's events, losses and score.","controls.command.turn_report.label":"Turn report","controls.command.undo.help":"Take back the last movement. Unavailable once the move revealed something: new spotting, a surprise or hidden enemy, an interception, or any combat.","controls.command.undo.label":"Undo move","controls.command.zoom_in.help":"One step closer, centred on what is already on screen.","controls.command.zoom_in.label":"Zoom in","controls.command.zoom_out.help":"One step further out, centred on what is already on screen.","controls.command.zoom_out.label":"Zoom out","controls.footer.close":"Press F1, ? or Esc to close.","controls.footer.manual":"Open the full manual","controls.group.general.title":"General","controls.group.map.title":"Map","controls.group.panels.title":"Panels","controls.group.unit.title":"Unit","controls.title":"Controls","dossier.awards.help":"Your Campaign Dossier's completed battles, grouped by the result earned. Hero medals are recorded separately in each commander's dossier.","dossier.awards.title":"Campaign Record","dossier.cas.aux_lost":"Own auxiliary lost","dossier.cas.core_lost":"Own core lost","dossier.cas.enemy_destroyed":"Enemy destroyed","dossier.cas.enemy_surrendered":"Enemy surrendered","dossier.casualties.title":"Combat Record \u2014 complete units, not strength points","dossier.defeat.title":"Defeat","dossier.finished":"CAMPAIGN FINISHED","dossier.subtitle":"Campaign Dossier","dossier.victory.title":"Victory","equipment.ability.air_drop_mines":"Air Drop Mines: can lay a land minefield from the air, on top of its Drop Mines ability.","equipment.ability.air_support":"Air Support: can supply air units the same way a friendly airfield does.","equipment.ability.allow_lof":"Allows Line of Fire: this formation never blocks a friendly line of fire. It matters only in scenarios where units block fire at all; elsewhere nothing blocks it and the ability changes nothing.","equipment.ability.anti_sub":"ASW (Anti-Submarine Warfare): may attack submarines, like a Destroyer or Tactical Bomber.","equipment.ability.bridge":"Bridge: acts as a bridge when standing in a river hex, letting other units cross.","equipment.ability.build_repair":"Sapper: can build a bridge, fortification, airfield or port, and repair what was destroyed.","equipment.ability.can_air_attack":"Can Attack Air: may attack aircraft despite not being an anti-air class.","equipment.ability.can_blow":"Can Blow: can demolish the bridge it stands on, or raze the terrain feature of its hex.","equipment.ability.cannot_attack_air":"Cannot attack aircraft, regardless of its air attack value.","equipment.ability.cannot_attack_hard":"Cannot attack armoured (hard) targets.","equipment.ability.cannot_attack_naval":"No Naval Attack: this equipment has no weapon that can engage a ship, whatever its naval attack value says.","equipment.ability.cant_buy":"Cannot Be Bought: never available for purchase. It reaches the field only as a scenario unit or an authored reinforcement.","equipment.ability.no_ai_buy":"Not Bought By The AI: available to you, but the computer opponent will never purchase it. It is usually equipment an author reserves for the player's side.","equipment.ability.no_prototype":"No Prototype: cannot be one of the early prototypes a brilliant victory awards, even when it is otherwise in date.","equipment.ability.air_transportable":"Air Transportable: may be carried by an air transport. A prime mover without it is left behind on the airfield when its formation is airlifted.","equipment.ability.cannot_attack_soft":"Cannot attack unarmoured (soft) targets.","equipment.ability.capture_flag":"Capture: may capture flagged objective hexes.","equipment.ability.carrier_deploy":"Carrier Deploy: may be deployed onto a friendly aircraft carrier, which is otherwise outside any deployment zone.","equipment.ability.clear_mines":"Clear Mines: can attempt to clear a land minefield while standing in it; a failed attempt suppresses it.","equipment.ability.cut_los":"Cuts Line of Sight: blocks ranged fire passing through this unit's hex, for both sides. Sight itself is not blocked.","equipment.ability.counter_battery":"Counterbattery: answers enemy artillery that fires on a friendly formation within range, once per turn.","equipment.ability.dismount":"Dismount: reverses whether this unit fights with its own statistics when attacked while riding a transport, instead of its transport's.","equipment.ability.dismount_after_move":"Dismount After Move: steps down from its transport automatically once its move ends, instead of riding until next turn.","equipment.ability.drop_mines":"Drop Mines: can lay a land minefield on its own hex - 2 ammunition, and no other action that turn.","equipment.ability.evade":"Evade: has a 50% chance of evading any attack, like a submarine.","equipment.ability.exploit_success":"Exploit Success: may move again after an attack that kills or routs the defender.","equipment.ability.ignores_entrenchment":"Ignores Entrenchment: attacking this unit gets no benefit from the defender's entrenchment level.","equipment.ability.jet_stealth":"Jet (Stealth): marked on jet aircraft; its exact effect is not documented anywhere, so do not assume one from the name.","equipment.ability.kamikaze":"Kamikaze: may sacrifice itself in a suicide attack.","equipment.ability.lasting_suppression":"Lasting Suppression: suppression it inflicts lasts until the end of the enemy's turn instead of clearing at the round wrap.","equipment.ability.marine":"Marine: trained for amphibious assault - keeps its movement after landing from a naval transport, instead of coming ashore spent.","equipment.ability.mechanized":"Mechanized: the crew rides its own prime mover, so the gun is exempt from having to fire before it moves.","equipment.ability.mountain":"Mountain: mountain-trained, so hills, rough ground and the mountains themselves cost it no more than dedicated mountain infantry pays.","equipment.ability.no_ammo_penalty":"No Ammo Penalty: does not suffer the usual penalty for defending without ammunition.","equipment.ability.no_dirt_airfields":"Cannot use dirt airfields: cannot refuel or deploy at an airfield defined as dirt, or one built by sappers during the scenario.","equipment.ability.no_intercept_air":"No Intercept Air: does not intercept aircraft moving through its range, though it still defends normally when attacked.","equipment.ability.no_leader":"No Leader: this equipment never produces a commander.","equipment.ability.no_need_station":"No Need Station: can board and leave a train anywhere on the track, with no railway station at either end.","equipment.ability.rail_transportable":"Rail Transportable: this formation may be carried by train. Emplaced anti-aircraft and permanent fortifications mostly cannot be.","equipment.ability.no_surrender":"No Surrender: never destroyed-as-surrendered when a forced retreat is impossible \u2014 fights on in place instead.","equipment.ability.no_zoc":"No Zone of Control: this unit does not slow or stop enemy formations moving past it.","equipment.ability.partizan":"Partizan: not stopped by adjacent enemies and cannot be caught by surprise.","equipment.ability.rocket_bomber":"Rocket Bomber: attacks ground targets at its full range rather than a reduced one.","equipment.ability.saboteur":"Saboteur: can sabotage enemy installations.","equipment.ability.single_fire_sup":"Single Fire Support: may give support fire only once per turn.","equipment.ability.supply_unit":"Supply Unit: acts as a mobile depot, resupplying adjacent friendly formations even if they have already moved or fired.","equipment.ability.torpedo_bomber":"Torpedo Bomber: attacks an adjacent unit with torpedoes if both are at sea.","equipment.ability.all_weather":"All Weather: not affected by weather \u2014 attacks, is attacked, and spots normally regardless of conditions.","equipment.action.buy.help":"Buy this equipment as a new unit. Prestige is spent now and the unit enters the reserve tray for deployment.","equipment.action.buy.label":"Buy","equipment.action.sell.help":"Permanently disband the selected unit and recover part of its prestige value.","equipment.action.sell.label":"Sell","equipment.action.sell.confirm.title":"Sell {unit}?","equipment.action.sell.confirm.confirm_button":"Sell","equipment.action.disband.confirm.title":"Disband {unit}?","equipment.action.disband.confirm.confirm_button":"Disband","equipment.action.sell_disband.confirm.body":"Refund: {refund} prestige<br>This permanently removes its experience, commander and attachments.","equipment.action.sell_disband.confirm.body_commander":"Refund: {refund} prestige<br>This permanently removes its experience, {commander}'s command, and attachments.","equipment.action.upgrade.help":"Upgrade the selected formation to this compatible model. You pay the cost difference and keep its identity, experience and hero.","equipment.action.upgrade.label":"Upgrade","equipment.all_classes":"All","equipment.all_countries":"All Countries","equipment.availability":"Available from {month} {year}","equipment.buy_blocked.campaign_country":"{selectedCountry} equipment \u2014 this campaign may only purchase {campaignCountry} equipment. It can still be upgraded from the Upgrade tab.","equipment.buy_blocked.campaign_no_purchase":"The campaign's author allows no purchases in this battle.","equipment.buy_blocked.no_anchor":"No supply hex or deployment zone in this scenario \u2014 nothing can be bought here (the enemy cannot buy either). Reinforcements arrive on schedule instead; capturing a port would open deployment.","equipment.buy_blocked.not_in_scenario_list":"This scenario limits what may be bought \u2014 its author picked a set of Fronts and Factions, and this equipment is outside it. Everything the list does allow is still on offer.","equipment.buy_blocked.purchase_cap":"This scenario caps how many NEW units you may add, and you have used every slot. Losses do not count against it \u2014 whenever a unit of yours is destroyed you may buy one more to replace it.","equipment.buy_blocked.transport_pool":"Air and naval transports are not bought in this scenario \u2014 the designer set a fixed pool of them, and a unit draws from that pool when it embarks. The pool size is shown on the transport panel.","equipment.buy_blocked.not_purchasable":"This transport is not marked as purchasable \u2014 it exists to be assigned to a unit, not bought as one. It can still be given to a unit as an organic transport.","equipment.card.inspect.help":"Select {name} to inspect its statistics, availability, price and special capabilities.","equipment.class_tab.air_defence.help":"Air defence and flak.","equipment.class_tab.air_defence.label":"Air def","equipment.class_tab.all.help":"Every class this side can field, in one list.","equipment.class_tab.all.label":"All","equipment.class_tab.anti_tank.help":"Anti-tank units.","equipment.class_tab.anti_tank.label":"Anti-tank","equipment.class_tab.artillery.help":"Artillery.","equipment.class_tab.artillery.label":"Artillery","equipment.class_tab.bombers.help":"Tactical and level bombers.","equipment.class_tab.bombers.label":"Bombers","equipment.class_tab.fighters.help":"Fighters and air transport.","equipment.class_tab.fighters.label":"Fighters","equipment.class_tab.fortification.help":"Fortifications and static emplacements.","equipment.class_tab.fortification.label":"Forts","equipment.class_tab.infantry.help":"Infantry and fortifications.","equipment.class_tab.infantry.label":"Infantry","equipment.class_tab.naval.help":"All naval classes: destroyers, submarines, cruisers, battleships, carriers and naval transport. Hidden on maps with no water.","equipment.class_tab.naval.label":"Naval","equipment.class_tab.recon.help":"Reconnaissance.","equipment.class_tab.recon.label":"Recon","equipment.class_tab.tanks.help":"Tanks and ground transport.","equipment.class_tab.tanks.label":"Tanks","equipment.cost.available":"Available Prestige:","equipment.cost.available_short":"Now:","equipment.cost.need_buy":"Need {amount} more prestige to buy.","equipment.cost.need_upgrade":"Need {amount} more prestige to upgrade.","equipment.country_cycle.help":"Cycle through equipment countries available to this side.","equipment.country.short":"Country","equipment.country_filter.help":"Filter the catalogue by equipment country. Campaign purchases may be restricted to the campaign nation.","equipment.detail.select_prompt":"Select a unit from the list to see its record.","equipment.detail.stat.0.help":"Attack power vs soft targets \u2014 infantry, artillery, unarmoured vehicles.","equipment.detail.stat.0.label":"Soft attack","equipment.detail.stat.1.help":"Attack power vs hard targets \u2014 tanks and other armoured vehicles.","equipment.detail.stat.1.label":"Hard attack","equipment.detail.stat.10.help":"How this unit moves \u2014 determines terrain cost, and whether it needs a road or is confined to the rail network.","equipment.detail.stat.10.label":"Movement type","equipment.detail.stat.11.help":"How many hexes away this unit reveals hidden enemies.","equipment.detail.stat.11.label":"Spotting","equipment.detail.stat.12.help":"Firing range in hexes (1 = must be adjacent).","equipment.detail.stat.12.label":"Range","equipment.detail.stat.13.help":"Rounds of ammunition before the unit must resupply.","equipment.detail.stat.13.label":"Ammo","equipment.detail.stat.14.help":"Fuel available before the unit must resupply.","equipment.detail.stat.14.label":"Fuel","equipment.detail.stat.2.help":"Attack power vs aircraft.","equipment.detail.stat.2.label":"Air attack","equipment.detail.stat.3.help":"Attack power vs ships \u2014 used when firing on naval targets, such as coastal guns or infantry engaging a landing craft.","equipment.detail.stat.3.label":"Naval attack","equipment.detail.stat.4.help":"Defence when attacked by a ground unit.","equipment.detail.stat.4.label":"Ground def","equipment.detail.stat.5.help":"Defence when attacked from the air.","equipment.detail.stat.5.label":"Air def","equipment.detail.stat.6.help":"Defence in close combat \u2014 when an adjacent enemy attacks at melee range, as opposed to ranged fire.","equipment.detail.stat.6.label":"Close def","equipment.detail.stat.7.help":"Defence bonus against ground fire from outside melee range \u2014 halved for an attacker within its own gun range, and waived against a moved Anti-Tank unit without a Tank Killer leader.","equipment.detail.stat.7.label":"Range def","equipment.detail.stat.8.help":"Higher initiative strikes first in combat, often before the enemy can return fire.","equipment.detail.stat.8.label":"Initiative","equipment.detail.stat.9.help":"Movement points per turn.","equipment.detail.stat.9.label":"Movement","equipment.heading":"{year} {class} upgrades for {country}","equipment.heading.purchase":"{year} \u00b7 {class} \u00b7 {country} \u2014 available to buy","equipment.heading.upgrade":"{year} \u00b7 {class} \u00b7 {country} \u2014 upgrades","equipment.heading.reserve":"{year} \u00b7 {class} \u00b7 {country} \u2014 reserve","equipment.mechanics.anti_air":"Anti-Air: when a friendly unit is attacked by aircraft, this unit fires on the attacking aircraft from up to its gun range away. It also intercepts enemy aircraft flying through its range while hidden, and \u2014 in scenarios that enable it \u2014 aircraft that end their move in range once spotted.","equipment.mechanics.headquarters":"Combat Support: lends this unit's experience bars to adjacent friendly units on the same air/ground layer. Multiple Combat Support units stack. It also gains a quarter of the combat experience earned by the units it supports.","equipment.mechanics.headquarters_bars":{"one":"Combat Support: currently lends {count} experience bar to adjacent friendly units on the same air/ground layer. Multiple Combat Support units stack. It also gains a quarter of the combat experience earned by the units it supports.","other":"Combat Support: currently lends {count} experience bars to adjacent friendly units on the same air/ground layer. Multiple Combat Support units stack. It also gains a quarter of the combat experience earned by the units it supports."},"equipment.mechanics.recon_movement":"Phased Movement: reconnaissance units may move again while movement points remain. Each movement segment spends points normally.","equipment.mechanics.support_fire":"Support Fire: when a friendly unit is attacked in close combat by a ground unit, this artillery fires on the attacker from up to its gun range away. It fires in addition to the defender, and does not have to be adjacent to either side.","equipment.mechanics.tank_overrun":"Overrun: if an attack on an adjacent hex is forecast to destroy the defender while the tank loses at most 1 strength and was not ambushed, no combat is fought: the defender is destroyed, the shot is not spent, and the tank may attack again. If it still had movement left, it may keep moving, with 1 extra point added to what remained. A tank that used all its movement before attacking can only fire after an overrun.","equipment.mode.purchase.help":"Purchase \u2014 browse equipment and buy a new unit for prestige. New units enter the reserve tray.","equipment.mode.purchase.label":"Purchase","equipment.mode.reserve.help":"Reserve \u2014 select purchased but undeployed units and place them on highlighted deployment hexes.","equipment.mode.reserve.label":"Reserve","equipment.mode.upgrade.help":"Upgrade \u2014 select one of your units, choose a compatible model, and pay the price difference.","equipment.mode.upgrade.label":"Upgrade","equipment.prestige.help":"Prestige available for purchases, upgrades and reinforcements.","equipment.refit.all.label":"Refit all ({units}) \u2014 {cost}","equipment.refit.all.help":"Restore {strength} strength across the whole reserve for {cost} prestige. Ammunition and fuel are restored free.","equipment.refit.all.partial.help":"Restoring the whole reserve needs {cost} prestige and you have {prestige}. The weakest formations will be refitted first, as far as your prestige reaches.","equipment.refit.unit.help":"Refit this formation: +{strength} strength for {cost} prestige{supply}.","equipment.refit.unit.supply":", plus free ammunition and fuel","equipment.refit.done":"Refit: +{strength} strength for {cost} prestige.","equipment.refit.short":"Not enough prestige to fully refit {units} formation(s).","equipment.reserve.commander.help":"Heroic commander: {rank} {name} \u2014 {renown}. Open the unit to read the full dossier.","equipment.reserve.auxiliary.label":"AUX","equipment.reserve.auxiliary.help":"Auxiliary unit: it fights in this battle only. It is not part of your core, does not carry over to the next battle, and refunds nothing when disbanded.","equipment.reserve.commander.settling":"Heroic commander: {rank} {name} \u2014 newly transferred. None of their traits apply to this formation for {turns} more turn(s).","equipment.reserve.empty":"No purchased units awaiting deployment.","equipment.reserve.hint":"Pick a unit, then click a highlighted deployment hex on the map. The window reopens until every reserve is placed.","equipment.sort.choose.help":"Choose the equipment statistic used to sort the catalogue.","equipment.sort.help":"Choose which equipment statistic orders the catalogue. Use the adjacent arrow to reverse the order.","equipment.sort.option":"Sort: {stat}","equipment.sort.reverse.help":"Reverse the catalogue sort order between lowest-to-highest and highest-to-lowest.","equipment.sort.short":"Sort.","equipment.sort.stat.air_attack":"Air attack","equipment.sort.stat.air_defence":"Air defence","equipment.sort.stat.ammo":"Ammo","equipment.sort.stat.close_defence":"Close defence","equipment.sort.stat.cost":"Cost","equipment.sort.stat.ground_defence":"Ground defence","equipment.sort.stat.hard_attack":"Hard attack","equipment.sort.stat.initiative":"Initiative","e