f your objectives, you lose at once.","hud.objective.threat.help":"The enemy was sent to capture these. The moment it holds every one of them, the battle ends in its victory, whatever turn it is.","hud.objective.tier.brilliant":"Brilliant victory","hud.objective.tier.by_turn":"by turn {turn}","hud.objective.tier.hold":{"one":"hold {count} objective","other":"hold {count} objectives"},"hud.objective.tier.missed":"passed (turn {turn})","hud.objective.tier.tactical":"Tactical victory","hud.objective.tier.victory":"Victory","hud.objective.tiers.help":"Capture every victory objective on or before the turn shown to earn that grade.","hud.objective.tiers.hold.enemy_capture":"The enemy is not bound by this: if it takes all the objectives it was sent to capture, you lose at once.","hud.objective.tiers.hold.help":"This scenario is graded on how many victory objectives you still hold when the turn limit runs out.","hud.objective.tiers.hold.no_early_end":"Capturing every objective does not end the battle early: the result is decided by the objectives you hold when turn {maxTurns} ends.","hud.objective.tiers.hold.title":"Turn-limit thresholds","hud.objective.tiers.title":"Victory deadlines","hud.observer.help":"Observer mode is active (fog of war disabled and/or hidden objectives shown) \u2014 affects game balance.","hud.observer.label":"OBSERVER","hud.options.help":"Options & menu (Esc) \u2014 save or load the game, change settings, or return to the battle.","hud.phase.deploy.help":"Initial deployment lasts until your first move or attack. During it, you can place reserve units and assign available commanders to formations. Reserve units can still be deployed later.","hud.phase.deploy.label":"DEPLOY","hud.phase.label":"Phase","hud.prestige.help":"Prestige \u2014 campaign resources spent on buying, upgrading and reinforcing units. The green value is next turn\u2019s income.","hud.prestige.value":"Prestige: {prestige}","hud.prestige.value_with_income":"Prestige: {prestige} (+{delta} next turn)","hud.ready_units.count.help":"Units still able to act this turn. Sleeping units are skipped by navigation.","hud.ready_units.help":"Ready units \u2014 the number of your units that can still move, attack or use another action this turn.","hud.ready_units.next.help":"Select and centre the next unit that can still act.","hud.ready_units.previous.help":"Select and centre the previous unit that can still act.","hud.reserves.help":"Reserves (R) \u2014 buy new units, upgrade existing formations, and deploy purchased units from the reserve tray.","hud.reserves.label":"Reserves","hud.status.location.aa_threat":"spotted AA threatens a unit that lands here, not one merely flying over it","hud.status.location.needs_transport":"too far on foot: the formation will mount its own transport and arrive riding","hud.status.location.field_airfield":"field airfield: some aircraft cannot refuel here","hud.status.location.help":"Hex under the pointer: terrain, road or place name, visible unit and map coordinates.","hud.save_status.saving":"Saving...","hud.save_status.saved":"Saved {time}","hud.save_status.failed":"Save failed","hud.save_status.session_only":"Not stored \u00b7 export a backup","hud.save_status.session_only.help":"This browser blocks site storage, so progress lasts only until the page closes. Click to download a backup file now.","hud.save_status.failed.export_now_help":"Saving failed - export a backup file with every campaign. Click to export now.","hud.status.scenario.help":"Current scenario, turn limit and in-game date. Victory tiers may require taking all objectives before an earlier turn threshold.","hud.strategic_map.help":"Strategic map (M) \u2014 toggle a whole-theatre overview for navigation. Unit actions are unavailable in this view.","hud.turn.label":"Turn","hud.turn.tooltip.title":"Turn {turn} of {maxTurns}","hud.turn.tooltip.remaining":{"one":"{count} turn left.","other":"{count} turns left."},"hud.turn.tooltip.last_turn":"This is the final turn.","hud.turn.tooltip.no_deadlines":"This scenario sets no victory deadline \u2014 the grade does not depend on how early you finish.","hud.turn_report.help":"Turn Report (L) \u2014 review objectives, score, prestige, combat results and recent events.","hud.turn_started":"Turn {turn}/{maxTurns} \u2014 {country} begins","hud.weather.effect.air_ground_halved":"Air-to-ground and ground-to-air fire strikes at half strength \u2014 flak included. A commander with All Weather Combat is unaffected.","hud.weather.effect.aircraft_free":"Aircraft operate freely \u2014 air attacks allowed.","hud.weather.effect.aircraft_grounded":"Aircraft cannot attack \u2014 grounded by the weather (they still defend themselves). A commander with All Weather Combat flies anyway.","hud.weather.effect.defense_bonus":"Every defender is 3 points harder to hurt.","hud.weather.effect.dry_movement":"Firm going \u2014 normal movement costs for all units.","hud.weather.effect.frozen_crossing":"Frozen rivers and swamps can be crossed by ground units.","hud.weather.effect.frozen_wheeled":"Wheeled transport struggles off-road (forests cost all movement).","hud.weather.effect.mud_movement":"Ground movement is much slower \u2014 wheeled vehicles bog down hardest.","hud.weather.effect.mud_swamps":"Swamps are impassable morass.","hud.weather.effect.rain_ground_change":"A few more turns of rain and the ground turns to mud; a few clear turns dry it out again.","hud.weather.effect.snow_ground_change":"A few more turns of snow and the ground freezes; it thaws back through mud, not straight to firm going.","hud.weather.effect.spotting_air":"Aircraft see half as far.","hud.weather.effect.spotting_ground":"Ground and naval units see half as far.","hud.weather.story.clear":"Clear skies over the front.","hud.weather.story.overcast":"Low cloud hangs over the battlefield.","hud.weather.story.rain":"Steady rain soaks the front.","hud.weather.story.snow":"Snow squalls sweep across the field.","hud.weather.tooltip.title":"{weather} \u00b7 {ground} ground","list.all_countries.label":"All countries","list.filter.country.help":"Filter by country (any side \u2014 including AI-only factions)","list.select_dossier.help":"Select {name} and show its full dossier.","list.group.toggle.help":"Click to open or close this campaign","list.sort.default.help":"Campaign order","list.sort.default.label":"Default","list.sort.name.help":"Alphabetical","list.sort.name.label":"A\u2013Z","list.sort.size.help":"Fewest operations first","list.sort.size.label":"Length","list.sort.year.help":"Earliest year first","list.sort.year.label":"Year","menu.language.label":"Language","menu.main.continue.label":"Continue","menu.main.continue.subtitle":"Resume your campaign","menu.main.restart_mission.label":"Restart Mission","menu.main.restart_mission.subtitle":"Return to the opening deployment","menu.main.restart_mission.confirm.title":"Restart this mission?","menu.main.restart_mission.confirm.body":"All progress made since the opening deployment will be lost.","menu.main.restart_mission.confirm.confirm_button":"Restart Mission","menu.main.restart_mission.failed":"The mission-start checkpoint is no longer available.","menu.main.restart_mission.unavailable":"Opening state not saved for this mission","menu.main.restart_mission.unavailable.body":"This browser has no saved opening state for the current mission, so it cannot be restarted. This happens for a mission started in an older version that was reloaded during its briefing, or whose opening the browser refused to store. Your current progress is unaffected; the next mission will have Restart Mission again.","menu.main.restart_mission.not_saved.title":"Restart Mission not saved","menu.main.restart_mission.not_saved.body":"The opening state of this mission could not be stored in this browser ({reason}). Restart Mission works until you close or reload this page, and a backup made now still contains it. After a reload this mission cannot be restarted.","menu.main.restart_mission.not_saved.session_only":"site storage is blocked","menu.main.hall_of_fame.label":"Hall of Fame","menu.main.hero_desk.label":"Hero Desk","menu.main.hero_desk.subtitle":"Commanders across your campaigns","menu.main.manual.label":"Field Manual","menu.main.manual.subtitle":"Rules and reference","menu.main.manual.help":"Open the field manual in a new tab: turn flow, combat, supply, commanders and the full reference tables.","menu.main.hero_desk.help":"Inspect every commander you have led: active officers from campaigns in progress, and the archived careers of the completed, retired and fallen.","menu.main.load_game.label":"Load Game","menu.main.load_game.subtitle":"Restore a saved battle","menu.main.new_campaign.label":"New Campaign","menu.main.new_campaign.subtitle":"Lead a nation through the war","menu.main.save_load.label":"Save / Load","menu.main.save_load.subtitle":"Save or restore a battle","menu.main.settings.label":"Settings","menu.main.settings.subtitle":"Options & display","menu.main.single_scenario.label":"Single Scenario","menu.main.single_scenario.subtitle":"Fight a standalone battle","menu.main.multiplayer.label":"Multiplayer","menu.main.multiplayer.subtitle":"Local two-tab cooperative game","menu.main.tagline":"Turn-based strategy of great battles","menu.main.about":"About","menu.main.privacy":"Privacy","menu.main.tutorial.label":"Tutorial","menu.main.tutorial.subtitle":"Learn the basics","menu.quotes.engels.army_economic_conditions.author":"F. Engels","menu.quotes.engels.army_economic_conditions.text":"Nothing is more dependent on economic conditions than precisely the army and the navy. Armament, composition, organization, tactics and strategy depend above all on the stage reached at the time in production.","menu.quotes.engels.mass_insurrection.author":"F. Engels","menu.quotes.engels.mass_insurrection.text":"Mass insurrection, revolutionary war, guerrilla detachments everywhere \u2014 this is the only method by which a small nation can overcome a large one.","menu.quotes.engels.new_military_methods.author":"F. Engels","menu.quotes.engels.new_military_methods.text":"The emancipation of the proletariat will have its own special expression in military affairs and will create its own, new military methods.","menu.quotes.lenin.attack_and_retreat.author":"V. I. Lenin","menu.quotes.lenin.attack_and_retreat.text":"Victory is impossible unless they have learned both how to attack and how to retreat properly.","menu.quotes.lenin.decisive_point.author":"V. I. Lenin","menu.quotes.lenin.decisive_point.text":"Concentrate a great superiority of forces at the decisive point.","menu.quotes.lenin.do_not_lay_down_arms.author":"V. I. Lenin","menu.quotes.lenin.do_not_lay_down_arms.text":"Once you have taken up arms, do not lay them down until the enemy is completely crushed.","menu.quotes.lenin.morale_decisive.author":"V. I. Lenin","menu.quotes.lenin.morale_decisive.text":"In modern war, the morale of the people is one of the decisive factors.","menu.quotes.lenin.peace_breathing_space.author":"V. I. Lenin","menu.quotes.lenin.peace_breathing_space.text":"Peace is a breathing-space for war.","menu.quotes.lenin.revolution_defend_itself.author":"V. I. Lenin","menu.quotes.lenin.revolution_defend_itself.text":"A revolution is only worth something if it can defend itself.","menu.quotes.lenin.war_politics.author":"V. I. Lenin","menu.quotes.lenin.war_politics.text":"War is the continuation of politics by other means.","menu.quotes.lenin.who_will_prevail.author":"V. I. Lenin","menu.quotes.lenin.who_will_prevail.text":"Who will prevail over whom \u2014 that is the fundamental question of every revolution.","menu.quotes.marx.change_the_world.author":"K. Marx","menu.quotes.marx.change_the_world.text":"The philosophers have only interpreted the world, in various ways; the point, however, is to change it.","menu.quotes.marx.force_midwife.author":"K. Marx","menu.quotes.marx.force_midwife.text":"Force is the midwife of every old society pregnant with a new one.","menu.quotes.marx.locomotives_of_history.author":"K. Marx","menu.quotes.marx.locomotives_of_history.text":"Revolutions are the locomotives of history.","menu.quotes.marx.weapon_of_criticism.author":"K. Marx","menu.quotes.marx.weapon_of_criticism.text":"The weapon of criticism cannot, of course, replace criticism of the weapon. Material force must be overthrown by material force.","menu.quotes.marx_engels.workers_unite.author":"K. Marx & F. Engels","menu.quotes.marx_engels.workers_unite.text":"Workers of the world, unite!","menu.quotes.stalin.artillery_god_of_war.author":"J. Stalin","menu.quotes.stalin.artillery_god_of_war.text":"Artillery is the god of war.","menu.quotes.stalin.master_all_forms.author":"J. Stalin","menu.quotes.stalin.master_all_forms.text":"The art of war in modern conditions consists in mastering all forms of warfare and in using them intelligently.","menu.quotes.stalin.no_fortresses.author":"J. Stalin","menu.quotes.stalin.no_fortresses.text":"There are no fortresses that Bolsheviks cannot storm.","menu.quotes.stalin.no_mercy.author":"J. Stalin","menu.quotes.stalin.no_mercy.text":"No mercy to the enemy!","menu.quotes.stalin.tactics_day.author":"J. Stalin","menu.quotes.stalin.tactics_day.text":"Tactics are the questions of the day, strategy the questions of the epoch.","menu.quotes.stalin.tactics_part_of_strategy.author":"J. Stalin","menu.quotes.stalin.tactics_part_of_strategy.text":"Tactics are a part of strategy, subordinate to it and serving it.","menu.quotes.stalin.victory_must_be_won.author":"J. Stalin","menu.quotes.stalin.victory_must_be_won.text":"Victory does not come by itself \u2014 it must be won.","menu.save.summary_full":"{name} \u00b7 Turn {turn}/{maxTurns}","menu.save.summary_short":"{name} \u00b7 Turn {turn}","multiplayer.rules.mismatch":"This room runs different rules ({rules}). Your fingerprint is {localHash}, the room's is {remoteHash}. Match the room's ruleset, or clear your own selection, to join.","multiplayer.rules.unknown":"This room uses rules this version of OSADA cannot run ({rules}). Update the game to join. Room fingerprint {remoteHash}.","multiplayer.rules.unsupported_schema":"This room uses an incompatible ruleset version. Update OSADA on both devices to join. Room fingerprint {remoteHash}.","rules.aa_intercept_mode.help":"Which anti-aircraft guns fire on aircraft within reach. Mode 0 is not \"off\": concealed guns already fire on aircraft moving through or stopping in range.","rules.aa_intercept_mode.label":"Anti-aircraft interception","rules.aa_intercept_mode.value.0":"Concealed guns intercept","rules.aa_intercept_mode.value.1":"Concealed guns intercept; a gun that fires cannot also air-defend","rules.aa_intercept_mode.value.2":"Concealed guns intercept; spotted guns intercept aircraft that stop in range","rules.aa_intercept_mode.value.3":"Spotted guns intercept aircraft that stop in range; a gun that fires cannot also air-defend","rules.action.delete.confirm.body":"\u201c{name}\u201d will be removed from your profile list. Saved games keep the exact rules they were played under.","rules.action.delete.confirm.title":"Delete ruleset profile?","rules.action.delete.help":"Delete this profile.","rules.action.delete.label":"Delete","rules.action.edit_copy.help":"Create a new profile starting from the current selection.","rules.action.edit_copy.label":"Edit copy\u2026","rules.action.rename.help":"Rename this profile. Saves and rooms that already use it keep working.","rules.action.rename.label":"Rename","rules.attachments.help":"Whether formations can be fitted with attachments at all. Turning them on cannot invent slots an equipment file never defined.","rules.attachments.label":"Attachments","rules.button.help":"Choose which ruleset this campaign or scenario runs under. Campaign rules lock when the campaign starts.","rules.button.help.locked":"These rules are already locked for this room or campaign. The window shows them read-only.","rules.locked.campaign_in_progress":"This campaign already has saved progress, so its ruleset was locked in when it started. Picking a different one here only takes effect on a new run \u2014 use \"Start over\" on this campaign, then reopen Rules before starting it.","rules.locked.multiplayer_guest":"The host has already set the rules for this room. You are viewing them read-only.","rules.button.label":"Rules","rules.editor.copy_name":"{name} (copy)","rules.editor.error.blank_name":"Give the profile a name.","rules.editor.error.duplicate_name":"You already have a profile with that name.","rules.editor.save.label":"Save","rules.editor.title":"Edit ruleset profile","rules.editor.title.rename":"Rename ruleset profile","rules.flak_range.help":"How far an anti-aircraft gun reaches, for interception and for supporting fire.","rules.flak_range.label":"Anti-aircraft reach","rules.flak_range.value":{"one":"{count} hex","other":"{count} hexes"},"rules.ground_change_turns.help":"How many turns in a row of the same sky it takes to move the ground one step. Three is the reading of \u201cseveral continuous turns\u201d this game runs on.","rules.ground_change_turns.label":"Turns of weather before the ground shifts","rules.ground_change_turns.value":{"one":"{count} turn","other":"{count} turns"},"rules.ground_follows_weather.help":"Whether a run of rain or snow turns the ground to mud or freezes it, which changes movement costs for every ground unit. Scenario authors set this per battle; a profile can override them.","rules.ground_follows_weather.label":"Weather changes the ground","rules.ground_follows_weather.value.0":"Never \u2014 the ground stays as the scenario set it","rules.ground_follows_weather.value.1":"As each scenario decides","rules.ground_follows_weather.value.2":"Always, even where the author switched it off","rules.hash.help":"Identifies these exact rules. Two players whose fingerprints match are running the same game.","rules.hash.label":"Ruleset fingerprint","rules.profile.aviation_trial":"Trial: Aircraft in Bad Weather","rules.profile.authors_vision":"Author's Vision","rules.profile.label":"Ruleset","rules.profile.name.label":"Profile name","rules.profile.newer_schema":"saved by a newer version (schema {version})","rules.profile.osada_default":"OSADA Default","rules.profile.unknown_rules":"uses rules this version cannot run ({rules})","rules.provenance.content_unavailable":"Requested, but this equipment file has no such mechanic","rules.provenance.custom_override":"Set by the selected profile","rules.provenance.not_open_general":"Not an Open General rule, so this profile leaves it off","rules.provenance.efile_default":"The equipment file says nothing, so the documented default applies","rules.provenance.efile_explicit":"Chosen by this content's equipment file","rules.provenance.osada_default":"The game's own baseline","rules.source.aviation_trial":"Follows the selected content, except that aircraft may attack in overcast, rain and snow. The existing weather penalties still apply: air-to-ground fire at half strength, and +3 defence in rain and snow. An experimental balance trial \u2014 not Open General's rule, whose manual keeps aircraft grounded.","rules.source.authors_vision":"Follows the configuration this content actually ships with.","rules.source.custom":"Your saved profile, laid over what this content ships with.","rules.source.osada_default":"OSADA's documented baseline, identical for every campaign and scenario.","rules.supply_model.help":"On: the per-terrain supply factors the equipment file itself defines. Off: one flat rule outside cities, which is what the five files that ship no terrain data run either way.","rules.supply_model.label":"Author's supply factors","rules.title":"Ruleset","rules.value.off":"Off","rules.value.on":"On","rules.value.requires":"Does nothing while \u201c{rule}\u201d is off","rules.value.unavailable":"Unavailable for this equipment file","rules.value.unknown":"Mode {value} (from the equipment file)","rules.weather_defense_bonus.help":"On: any unit being attacked gains 3 points of defence in rain or snow, on land, at sea and in the air alike. Overcast does not grant it.","rules.weather_defense_bonus.label":"Rain and snow favour every defender","rules.weather_grounds_aircraft.help":"On: aircraft cannot start an attack in overcast, rain or snow, though they still defend themselves. Ground and naval units are unaffected by this one. A commander with All Weather Combat is exempt either way.","rules.weather_grounds_aircraft.label":"Bad weather grounds aircraft","rules.weather_halves_air_ground.help":"On: any attack that crosses the air/ground boundary uses half its strength points in bad weather \u2014 that is anti-aircraft guns firing upward as much as aircraft striking down. Combat within one layer is unaffected.","rules.weather_halves_air_ground.label":"Bad weather halves fire between air and ground","rules.weather_halves_spotting.help":"On: aircraft see half as far in any weather worse than fair, and ground and naval units see half as far in rain or snow.","rules.weather_halves_spotting.label":"Bad weather shortens sight for everyone","scenario.back.help":"Return to the main menu without starting a scenario.","scenario.counter":{"one":"{count} scenario","other":"{count} scenarios"},"scenario.filter.placeholder":"Filter scenarios\u2026","scenario.select.help":"Choose a standalone battle; its briefing and playable sides appear below.","scenario.selection.title":"Scenario Selection","scenario.tutorial.title":"Tutorial \u2014 Khalkhin Gol","scenario.tutorial.description":"Tutorial \u2014 Khalkhin Gol<br>3 July 1939<br><br>Japanese forces have crossed the Khalkhin Gol and occupied positions around the Bain-Tsagan heights.<br><br><b>What you will learn</b><br>For the first three turns the game fights the battle for you and shows one mechanic at a time:<br>\u2022 objectives<br>\u2022 unit information<br>\u2022 transport<br>\u2022 reconnaissance<br>\u2022 artillery preparation<br>\u2022 support fire<br>\u2022 reinforcement<br>\u2022 resupply<br>\u2022 OverRun<br>At the start of turn 4, full command of the Soviet-Mongolian detachment passes to you.<br><br><b>Your task</b><br>\u2022 Capture the Khaylastyn Crossing.<br>\u2022 Capture the Hamar-Daba Command Post.<br>\u2022 Optional: take the Bain-Tsagan Observation Point.","scenario.cubali01.title":"Sierra Maestra 1958","scenario.cubali01.description":"Oriente Province, spring 1958. Eighteen months after the yacht Granma put 82 men ashore, Fidel Castro's 26th of July Movement holds the high Sierra Maestra and little else. In Havana, Batista is gathering more than ten thousand soldiers, with tanks and aircraft, for the offensive meant to finish the rebels for good: Operation Verano.<br><br>Don't wait for it. Come down from the mountains, overrun the garrisons, seize the sugar mills and cut the roads to Bayamo and Manzanillo. Every town you take is one the army must fight to win back. How far can a guerrilla army reach before the blow lands? Far enough for Santiago de Cuba?<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection. Special thanks to JML and Paqueo for testing.","scenario.battle_cuito.title":"Battle of Cuito Cuanavale (1987)","scenario.battle_cuito.description":"South-east Angola, December 1987. The FAPLA offensive against UNITA-held Mavinga has ended in disaster. South African guns and armour caught its brigades on the Lomba River, and the survivors have fallen back on Cuito Cuanavale, the town that anchors the whole southern front.<br><br>In Havana, Fidel Castro has decided that Cuito will not fall. Cuban tank crews, gunners and pilots are on their way, and General Arnaldo Ochoa has taken command. Stop the rout, then turn it around and carry the war back to Mavinga. The fighting that follows is often called the largest battle in Africa since the Second World War, and its echoes will reach all the way to Namibian independence.<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection.","scenario.amilastc_sfb.title":"Amin's Last Chance (1979)","scenario.amilastc_sfb.description":"Uganda, March 1979. Idi Amin's invasion of Tanzania's Kagera Salient has backfired. President Nyerere has answered with a counter-invasion, and the Tanzanian army and Ugandan exiles are across the border and driving on Kampala.<br><br>Amin's last hope is his friend in Tripoli. Muammar Gaddafi is flying Libyan troops, armour and Katyusha rocket launchers into Entebbe to stop the invaders on the Kampala road. Command the defenders and hold as much ground as you can for as long as you can. Historically, the Libyan counterattack broke at Lukaya, and Kampala fell on 11 April. This is the other side of Victory at Kampala: the same war, seen from inside a collapsing regime.<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection.","scenario.1954_dienbienphu.title":"1954 Battle of Dien Bien Phu","scenario.1954_dienbienphu.description":"North-west Tonkin, spring 1954. The French built their fortress in a valley near the Laotian border, certain that no Viet Minh army could bring artillery through the jungle mountains around it. General V\u00f5 Nguy\u00ean Gi\u00e1p's soldiers and porters did it anyway. They dragged guns by hand onto the heights and moved supplies on bicycles.<br><br>B\u00e9atrice and Gabrielle fell in the first days of the siege in March, and French aircraft can no longer land. What is left are the Legionnaires and paratroopers in Dominique, Eliane, Claudine, Fran\u00e7oise and the southern outpost of Isabelle, with a handful of tanks. Close the ring and finish it. The garrison surrendered on 7 May 1954. The next day, the Geneva Conference turned to Indochina.","scenario.khalkin1.title":"Khalkhin Gol 1 - Japanese Attack (1939)","scenario.khalkin1.description":"The Mongolian steppe, early July 1939. After weeks of border clashes near Nomonhan, the Kwantung Army has decided to \"expel the invaders\". On the night of 2\u20133 July, Lieutenant General Komatsubara's infantry crossed the Khalkhin Gol on a single pontoon bridge and took Bain-Tsagan hill on the west bank. At the same time, General Yasuoka's tanks struck the Soviet bridgehead on the east bank.<br><br>If the Japanese hold Bain-Tsagan, every Soviet and Mongolian unit across the river is cut off. Komdiv Georgy Zhukov cannot wait for his infantry. He sends his tank and armoured-car brigades straight off the march against the hill. Drive the Japanese back over the river before they dig in.","scenario.khalkin2.title":"Khalkhin Gol 2 - Zhukov's Strike (1939)","scenario.khalkin2.description":"20 August 1939, 05:45. For six weeks the two armies have faced each other across the Khalkhin Gol. Zhukov, now commanding the new 1st Army Group, has used them to hide a build-up. He sent fake radio traffic about digging in for the winter, played the noise of pile drivers and engines over loudspeakers, and moved tanks only at night. Meanwhile the Japanese plan an offensive of their own for 24 August.<br><br>Strike first. After the artillery and hundreds of aircraft have done their work, pin the 23rd Division in the centre while the tank brigades on both flanks swing around behind it. Close the pincers at Nomonhan before the enemy understands what is happening. The defeat will weigh on Tokyo two years later, when it chooses to strike south rather than at the Soviet Union.","scenario.sparta.title":"Spartacist Uprising - Berlin (1919)","scenario.sparta.description":"Berlin, 5 January 1919. Two months after the revolution toppled the Kaiser, Friedrich Ebert's government has sacked Emil Eichhorn, the left-wing police chief. Crowds pour into the streets. Armed workers occupy the newspaper quarter around Kochstra\u00dfe, and Karl Liebknecht and the Revolutionary Stewards form a committee to overthrow the government.<br><br>Ebert has given Gustav Noske the job of restoring order. \"Someone has to be the bloodhound,\" Noske says, and he calls in the Freikorps: the Reinhard brigade from the north, volunteers from Potsdam and the Garde-Kavallerie-Sch\u00fctzen-Division from the south. Take the Reichstag and strike at their bases before they close in. Historically, the rising was crushed within a week. On 15 January, officers of that same Guard Cavalry division murdered Liebknecht and Rosa Luxemburg.<br><br>Historical liberties: the People's Navy Division (Volksmarinedivision), which stayed out of the January fighting, fights here, and the cavalry from F\u00fcrstenwalde and Freienwalde is invented for balance.","scenario.madrid_36.title":"Defence of Madrid (1936)","scenario.madrid_36.description":"Madrid, November 1936. Franco's Army of Africa has marched up the Tagus valley almost unchecked, and General Varela's columns stand in the Casa de Campo and at the bridges over the Manzanares. The government has left for Valencia. Everyone expects the capital to fall within days. General Mola boasts of a \"fifth column\" already waiting inside the city.<br><br>Madrid decides otherwise. General Miaja's defence junta, the militias, the first Mixed Brigades of the new People's Army and the International Brigades, who marched down the Gran V\u00eda on 8 November, hold the line at the University City and the Puente de los Franceses. \u00a1No pasar\u00e1n! Keep them out of Madrid. Historically, the city held for almost two and a half more years.","scenario.mallorca.title":"Landing on Mallorca (1936)","scenario.mallorca.description":"Balearic Islands, August 1936. Menorca stayed loyal to the Republic, but Mallorca went over to the rebels in the first days of the war. Captain Alberto Bayo, an air force officer, sets out from Barcelona with Catalan militia and volunteers to win it back. On 16 August his troops come ashore on the east coast around Porto Cristo, supported by warships and seaplanes.<br><br>Secure the east-coast harbours, then drive inland on Manacor, Inca and Palma before the Nationalists recover and Italian aircraft arrive. Historically, the bridgehead stalled and was evacuated in early September. Bayo's story does not end here: twenty years later, in Mexico, he trained the men of Fidel Castro's Granma expedition.","scenario.teruel.title":"Battle of Teruel (1937)","scenario.teruel.description":"Aragon, December 1937. Teruel juts into Republican territory like a gun pointed at the Levante coast, and Franco is massing his army for a new offensive against Madrid. The Republic strikes first to stop it. On 15 December the People's Army attacks in a blizzard, in the coldest Spanish winter in decades, with temperatures falling to around \u221220 \u00b0C.<br><br>Encircle the city, beat off the relief columns and take Teruel street by street. Colonel Rey d'Harcourt's garrison held out in the seminary and the Bank of Spain until 8 January. Teruel was the only provincial capital the Republic ever took from the rebels. Then Franco's counteroffensive came, and the battle became one of the bloodiest of the war.","scenario.ebro.title":"Battle of the Ebro (1938)","scenario.ebro.description":"Catalonia, 25 July 1938. After the disasters of the winter and spring, the Republic has been cut in two and is widely written off abroad. The rebel advance through the Levante is driving on Valencia. The Republic needs a feat of arms to prove it is still alive.<br><br>Before dawn, Juan Modesto's Army of the Ebro crosses the river in boats and on pontoon bridges between Mequinenza and Amposta and falls on the Nationalist rear. Take Gandesa and the heights around it, then hold what you have taken against crushing rebel superiority in aircraft and artillery. Historically, Gandesa never fell. The battle lasted 115 days, the longest of the war, and was the last fight of the International Brigades.","scenario.partisanen.title":"Yugoslav Partisans - Operation Weiss (1943)","scenario.partisanen.description":"Dalmatia, February 1943. On the mainland, the Axis has launched Case White, its largest offensive yet against Tito's Partisans. Across the channel from Split, on the island of Bra\u010d, local Partisans have spent months raiding the occupiers and ferrying men and supplies to the coast. Now a regiment of German mountain troops has landed and taken the harbours.<br><br>Come down from the hills, retake Postira, Milna and Mirca, and throw the Gebirgsj\u00e4ger back into the sea. This is a what-if. In 1943 Bra\u010d was under Italian occupation, and German troops came to the island only after Italy's surrender.","scenario.aran.title":"Val d'Aran Invasion (1944)","scenario.aran.description":"The Pyrenees, October 1944. France is almost free, and thousands of Spanish Republicans who fought in the French Resistance believe Franco will be next. The communist-led Spanish National Union sends some four thousand guerrillas over the mountains into the Val d'Aran, a valley on the northern slope that the winter snows cut off from the rest of Spain.<br><br>The plan is to take Vielha, proclaim a provisional Republican government on Spanish soil, spark a popular rising and draw the Allies into finishing Franco off. Take the valley and the roads south before the army's reinforcements arrive. Historically, no rising came. Franco rushed tens of thousands of troops north, and after ten days Santiago Carrillo ordered the retreat. Can you do better?","scenario.op_hooper.title":"Operation Hooper - Cuito Cuanavale (1987)","scenario.op_hooper.description":"Cuito Cuanavale, the turn of 1988. The South African Defence Force has chased the beaten FAPLA brigades back to the Cuito River. In Operation Hooper it means to finish them by destroying the forces still east of the river and, if it can, taking the town.<br><br>This time the defenders are not alone. Cuban tanks and artillery have arrived, Cuban MiG-23s contest the sky, and the Tumpo bridgehead has been ringed with minefields and gun lines. Bleed the South African assaults dry, then strike back toward Mavinga. Pretoria's army left Cuito without the town, and within months Cuban columns were advancing on the Namibian border.<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection.","scenario.vkampala_sfb.title":"Victory at Kampala (1979)","scenario.vkampala_sfb.description":"Uganda, March 1979. Idi Amin invaded Tanzania's Kagera Salient last autumn. President Julius Nyerere answered in a way nobody expected, with a counter-invasion. The Tanzania People's Defence Force, with Ugandan exiles at its side, has crossed the border and is driving on the capital.<br><br>Amin has called in his ally Muammar Gaddafi, and Libyan troops are landing at Entebbe. Break them at Lukaya, take Entebbe and its airport, and march into Kampala. The capital fell on 11 April 1979, and Amin fled into exile.<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection.","scenario.1920_perekop.title":"1920 Siege of Perekop","scenario.1920_perekop.description":"Northern Tavria, November 1920. Poland has signed an armistice, and the Red Army can at last turn its full weight on the last White army in European Russia. Baron Wrangel's troops have fallen back into the Crimea behind the Perekop isthmus. They hold the old Turkish Wall, a rampart the height of a three-storey house fronted by a deep ditch, with the Ishun lines behind it.<br><br>Frunze's Southern Front will storm Perekop head-on while other columns wade the freezing shallows of the Sivash to turn the defences. Makhno's Black Army, allied with the Reds against Wrangel, fights under your command. Break through, take Armyansk and Ishun, and open the road into the Crimea. Within days the Crimea was free, and what remained of the last White army had fled abroad by sea.","scenario.side.additional_nations":{"one":"{count} additional nation fighting on this side","other":"{count} additional nations fighting on this side"},"scenario.side.ai_controlled":"AI CONTROLLED","scenario.side.also_fighting":"Also fighting on this side: {countries}","scenario.side.choose":"Choose your side","scenario.side.number":"Side {number}","scenario.side.play_as.help":"Play this scenario as {country}. The opposing side will be controlled by the AI.","scenario.side.player":"\u2713 PLAYER","scenario.side.select":"SELECT SIDE","scenario.side.start_as":"Start as {country}","scenario.side.unavailable.help":"{country} is not available as a human-controlled side in this scenario.","scenario.side.vs":"VS","scenario.start.help":"Start the selected standalone battle with the chosen human side.","scenario.start.label":"Start Scenario","scenario.status.new":"New","scenario.status.played":"Played","selection.authors.label":{"one":"Author","other":"Authors"},"selection.authors.role.adaptation":"adaptation","selection.authors.role.conversion":"conversion","selection.authors.role.original":"original author","selection.authors.role.translation":"translation","settings.done.help":"Apply these settings and return. Some display-resolution changes require a page reload.","settings.gameplay.confirm_end_turn.help":"Asks for confirmation before ending the turn and warns when units still have actions available.","settings.gameplay.confirm_end_turn.label":"Confirm end of turn","settings.gameplay.optional_objectives.help":"Shows name labels over non-objective owned hexes such as towns and airfields.","settings.gameplay.optional_objectives.label":"Show optional objectives tooltips","settings.gameplay.quick_animation.help":"Shortens movement and combat animations. Rules and results are unchanged.","settings.gameplay.quick_animation.label":"Quick combat and move animations","settings.gameplay.stalin_regime.help":"Multiplies the local player's unit attack, defence, initiative, movement, range, ammunition and fuel stats, and all positive prestige income, by 10. Spotting range is not changed, so fog of war still applies.","settings.gameplay.stalin_regime.label":"STALIN REGIME","settings.language.help":"Choose the interface language. The game updates immediately without reloading the current battle.","settings.map.enhanced_side_markers.help":"On the Strategic Map, adds a star to your side's unit flags and a skull to the enemy's, so allegiance does not depend on flag colour alone. National flags are unchanged, and units hidden by fog of war stay hidden.","settings.map.enhanced_side_markers.label":"Enhanced side markers","settings.map.mark_enemy_hexes.label":"Shade enemy units on map","settings.map.mark_enemy_hexes.help":"Darkens the hex under each spotted enemy unit. Units hidden by fog of war are not revealed.","settings.map.mark_enemy_units.help":"Uses red strength markers for spotted enemy units. This does not reveal units hidden by fog of war.","settings.map.mark_enemy_units.label":"Mark enemy strength in red","settings.map.mark_own_units.help":"Adds a clear marker beneath your units so stacked sprites and aircraft are easier to distinguish.","settings.map.mark_own_units.label":"Mark own units on map","settings.map.show_grid_terrain.help":"Colours each hex by terrain type when the Grid overlay is enabled, making movement terrain easier to read.","settings.map.show_grid_terrain.label":"Show terrain with Hex Grid","settings.map.use_retina.help":"Renders the map at the display's full device-pixel resolution. Sharper on high-DPI screens, but uses more graphics memory and requires a reload.","settings.map.use_retina.label":"Zoom to full device resolution","settings.observer.hidden_victory_hexes.help":"Reveals secret objectives that have no flag on the map. Most scenarios have none; regular bordered objectives are always visible. This changes game balance.","settings.observer.hidden_victory_hexes.label":"Show hidden victory hexes","settings.observer.no_fow.help":"Removes fog of war and reveals all enemy units. This changes game balance.","settings.observer.no_fow.label":"Disable Fog of War","settings.section.gameplay.title":"Gameplay","settings.section.map_view.title":"Map View","settings.section.observer.caption":"Affects game balance","settings.section.observer.locked_multiplayer":"Disabled in multiplayer","settings.section.observer.locked_multiplayer.help":"Observer Mode is unavailable during a multiplayer match: it would give one player information or combat strength the other does not have. These settings return when the match ends.","settings.section.observer.title":"Observer Mode","settings.section.sound.title":"Sound","settings.slider.ambient_volume.help":"Volume for continuous ambient audio such as rain and wind.","settings.slider.ambient_volume.label":"Ambient volume","settings.slider.music_volume.help":"Volume for the scenario's own music track, where its author wrote one. Independent of the ambient weather loop.","settings.slider.music_volume.label":"Music volume","settings.slider.effects_volume.help":"Volume for movement, weapon and combat sound effects.","settings.slider.effects_volume.label":"Effects volume","settings.slider.interface_scale.help":"Scales menus, panels and HUD controls without changing the tactical map zoom.","settings.slider.interface_scale.label":"Interface scale","settings.slider.interface_width.help":"Legacy interface-width value retained for compatibility; the current HUD automatically follows the viewport.","settings.slider.interface_width.label":"Interface width (px)","settings.slider.map_scale.help":"Scales the tactical map and unit sprites. This is the same zoom controlled beneath the minimap.","settings.slider.map_scale.label":"Game Map scale","settings.sound.mute_unit_sounds.help":"Mutes discrete movement, weapon and combat sounds. Ambient weather audio has its own volume control.","settings.sound.mute_unit_sounds.label":"Mute unit combat sounds","tutorial.command.body":"<b>Well done, Commander.</b><br><br>The three-turn demonstration is complete. The next Soviet turn is yours.<br><br>Capture the Hamar-Daba Command Post to win. Bain-Tsagan Observation Point is optional.<br><br>Scout first, soften entrenched defenders with artillery, and use armour to exploit the breach.","tutorial.command.title":"You Are Now in Command","tutorial.sides":"{left} vs {right}","tutorial.sides.commanded":"{left} vs {right} \u2014 you command the {commanded}","tutorial.turn1.complete":"The first demonstration turn is complete. A scenario is lost if its primary objectives are not taken before the final turn shown on the top bar.","tutorial.turn1.hamar_daba":"Hamar-Daba is the second primary objective. Both primary objectives must be held to win, and capturing them awards prestige for reinforcement, upgrades, and new units.","tutorial.turn1.optional_objective":"Bain-Tsagan Observation Point is optional: it is not required for victory, but it offers extra prestige, experience, and a useful forward position.","tutorial.turn1.primary_crossing":"Primary objectives have an enemy flag inside a golden frame. Capture this crossing by moving one of your ground units onto the hex after its defender has been removed.","tutorial.turn1.recon":"The BA-10 is a reconnaissance unit. Recon has a larger spotting range and may move in several stages, making it ideal for revealing ambushes before slower units advance.","tutorial.turn1.strength":"The number beside a unit is its strength. It represents how much of the formation remains combat-effective. The colour and small status markers also show whether the unit has moved or fired during the current turn.","tutorial.turn1.terrain":"Roads are usually fastest, while hills, rivers, marshes, and rough ground reduce movement in different ways. Scout first, then commit the tanks and infantry.","tutorial.turn1.transport":"This machine-gun battalion has truck transport. Press the truck button to mount or dismount it: <span class=\"osada-inline-glyph\" aria-hidden=\"true\">[</span><br>Transport greatly improves movement on roads, but mounted units are vulnerable. Infantry automatically dismounts when attacked.","tutorial.turn1.unit_info":"Selecting a unit opens its Unit Info card in the lower-left corner. Press <b>ALL STATS</b> to expand movement, spotting, attack, defence, ammunition, fuel, experience, and entrenchment. Highlighted hexes show the unit\u2019s current movement range.","tutorial.turn2.artillery":"The crossing is held by entrenched infantry. Artillery attacks from range, normally avoids return fire, and reduces entrenchment \u2014 this is artillery preparation or softening.","tutorial.turn2.bombardment":"That was a real bombardment: the defender lost strength and/or entrenchment, ammunition was spent, and both formations gained combat experience. Prepared positions should be softened before a close assault.","tutorial.turn2.combat_estimate":"Before attacking, the combat cursor estimates losses for both sides. Treat the estimate as a warning rather than a promise: terrain, experience, entrenchment, initiative, and support fire can all change the result.","tutorial.turn2.counterattack":"The Japanese counterattack forced the transported infantry to dismount automatically. The nearby Soviet battery also provided support fire: artillery may fire automatically when a friendly ground unit inside its range is attacked.","tutorial.turn2.target_types":"Infantry and artillery are soft targets; tanks are hard targets. Different weapons use different attack values against them. The BT-5 is now positioned to exploit the weakened line next turn.","tutorial.turn3.crossing_captured":"Khaylastyn Crossing has been captured. The flag changes to your side and the prestige award is added to the top bar. Early objective captures also improve the final score.","tutorial.turn3.overrun_result":"<b>OverRun!</b> The weakened unit was destroyed and the BT-5 remains able to continue its advance. OverRun is the reward for preparing the attack and committing armour at the right moment.","tutorial.turn3.overrun_setup":"The artillery preparation has left the forward company at breaking point. A tank attacking an adjacent unit can score an OverRun when it destroys the defender while suffering no more than one loss.","tutorial.turn3.reinforcement":"Reinforcement restores lost strength and costs prestige. Enemy units nearby reduce the result, and a reinforced unit cannot move or attack again during that turn.","tutorial.turn3.resupply":"Units consume ammunition and, when motorised, fuel. A unit without ammunition cannot attack, and a motorised unit without fuel cannot move. Press the barrel button to restore both: <span class=\"osada-inline-glyph\" aria-hidden=\"true\">!</span>","tutorial.welcome.body":"Tutorial \u2014 Khalkhin Gol<br>3 July 1939<br>Japanese forces have crossed the Khalkhin Gol and occupied positions around the Bain-Tsagan heights. The first three turns are an AI-controlled demonstration of objectives, unit information, transport, reconnaissance, artillery preparation, support fire, reinforcement, resupply, and OverRun. At the start of turn 4, full control of the Soviet-Mongolian detachment passes to you. Capture the Khaylastyn Crossing and the Hamar-Daba Command Post; the Bain-Tsagan Observation Point is optional.","tutorial.welcome.title":"Tutorial \u2014 Khalkhin Gol","unit_info.action.disembark.help":"Leaves the transport onto an adjacent hex.","unit_info.action.dismount.help":"Unloads the formation from its organic ground transport.","unit_info.action.dismount.label":"Dismount","unit_info.action.effect.lay_minefield":"Lays a minefield here for {amount} ammunition","unit_info.action.effect.open_barrage_targeting":"Opens barrage targeting - {amount} hexes in reach","unit_info.action.embark.help":"Boards air or naval transport at this facility.","unit_info.action.embark.label":"Embark","unit_info.action.engineering.blocked":"This formation cannot do that here.","unit_info.action.barrage.blocked":"That hex cannot be shelled from here.","unit_info.action.barrage.done.bridge":"Barrage: the bridge is down","unit_info.action.barrage.done.hit":"Barrage on target - nothing there to wreck","unit_info.action.barrage.done.miss":"Barrage fell wide","unit_info.action.barrage.done.rail":"Barrage: the railway is cut","unit_info.action.barrage.done.crater":"Barrage: craters left in the open ground","unit_info.action.barrage.done.rubble":"Barrage: wreckage left behind","unit_info.action.barrage.done.wrecked":"Barrage: reduced to rubble until repaired","unit_info.action.barrage.help":"Shell a hex within this formation's gun range - an unseen one, or a visible one with no ground unit in it; aircraft bomb the hex beneath them. A hit takes strength, ammunition, fuel and two levels of entrenchment off anything hidden there, or wrecks a city, airfield, port or bridge until engineers repair it - leaving ground that costs more to cross; open ground is cratered when that rule is on. Which cover and works may be wrecked is the equipment file's decision. Costs one ammunition point and the formation's shot, whether or not it lands.","unit_info.action.barrage.label":"Barrage","unit_info.action.barrage.pick":"Pick a hex to shell. Press Barrage again to cancel.","unit_info.action.rail_move.help":"Board a train here. The formation travels as the train \u2014 along the track only, with the train's movement and defence \u2014 until it steps off at a station.","unit_info.action.rail_move.label":"Entrain","unit_info.action.reason.no_barrage_target":"There is no hex in reach that can be shelled.","unit_info.action.lay_mines.blocked":"This formation cannot lay mines here.","unit_info.action.lay_mines.done":"Minefield laid","unit_info.action.lay_mines.help":"Lay a minefield on this hex. Costs two ammunition points and the formation's whole turn, and it must not have moved, fired or resupplied first. Your own units cross your minefields freely.","unit_info.action.lay_mines.label":"Lay mines","unit_info.action.mount.help":"Loads the formation onto its own organic ground transport.","unit_info.action.mount.label":"Mount","unit_info.action.overstrength.help":"Raises an experienced formation above its normal strength.","unit_info.action.overstrength.label":"Overstr.","unit_info.action.reason.scenario_forbids_engineering":"This mission forbids this kind of engineering work","unit_info.action.reason.engineering_in_progress":"Work is already under way on this hex","unit_info.action.reason.bridge_needs_crossing":"A bridge can only be built on a river or stream hex with no bridge yet","unit_info.action.reason.fortification_needs_ground":"A fortification needs dry ground that is not already fortified; forest and mountains only where the equipment file allows building there","unit_info.action.reason.airfield_needs_clear":"A field airfield can only be laid out on clear terrain","unit_info.action.reason.port_needs_coast":"A port needs dry ground on the coast, and no port here already","unit_info.action.reason.station_needs_rail":"A station can only be built on a railway hex that has none","unit_info.action.reason.engineering_needs_unspent_turn":"Engineering work needs a formation that has not yet moved, fired or resupplied this turn","unit_info.action.reason.engineering_needs_unfired":"Engineering work needs a formation that has not yet fired or resupplied this turn","unit_info.action.reason.minefield_already_here":"This hex already carries your minefield.","unit_info.action.reason.mines_need_unspent_turn":"A formation must have taken no other action this turn to lay mines.","unit_info.action.reason.no_minefield_here":"There is no minefield on this hex.","unit_info.action.reason.not_enough_ammo_for_mines":"Needs {amount} more ammunition to lay a minefield.","unit_info.action.reinforce.help":"Buys replacements for lost strength and resupplies the formation. When Reinforce offers veterans and recruits, veterans keep the formation's experience.","unit_info.action.reinforce.label":"Reinforce","unit_info.action.repair.help":"Rebuild what was destroyed here - the terrain feature a demolition razed, a bridge that was blown, a cut railway line - and level the wreckage and shell craters left behind. Duration and when work may begin are listed below, from the rules in force; the countdown runs at the end of each of your turns, this one included, while an engineer stays on the hex.","unit_info.action.repair.label":"Repair","unit_info.action.resupply.help":"Restores ammunition and fuel from local supply.","unit_info.action.resupply.label":"Resupply","unit_info.action.cautious.label":"Cautious","unit_info.action.cautious.help":"Moves only through hexes your side can see. Selecting another unit turns it off.","unit_info.action.effect.cautious_route":"Move range and route will use spotted hexes only. A concealed enemy can still be met on a spotted hex.","unit_info.action.effect.normal_route":"Back to the ordinary move range.","controls.command.cautious.label":"Cautious move (spotted hexes only)","controls.command.cautious.help":"Toggle a move range restricted to hexes your side can see, for the selected unit. Shift+click selects a unit straight into this mode; holding Shift with a unit selected switches it on while the key is down and marks the route to the hex under the pointer.","unit_info.action.sleep.help":"Skips this formation in ready-unit navigation for the rest of the turn.","unit_info.action.sleep.label":"Sleep","unit_info.action.undo.help":"Rewinds this formation\u2019s most recent move.","unit_info.action.undo.label":"Undo","unit_info.action.withdraw.label":"Withdraw","unit_info.action.cover_enter.label":"Take cover","unit_info.action.cover_enter.help":"Move this formation inside the friendly fortification on or beside its hex. Inside it cannot be seen or attacked on its own and is resupplied at the start of every round; where the equipment file allows it, artillery, anti-aircraft guns and staff inside still support the fortification and its neighbours. It can come out again from your next turn, onto a free hex beside the fortification. If the fortification is destroyed, everything inside is lost with it.","unit_info.action.cover.label":"Garrison","unit_info.action.cover.help":"Open this fortification's garrison: see which formations are inside, their ammunition and fuel, and order one to come out onto a free hex beside it. Friendly land formations go in with Take cover from this hex or the six around it.","unit_info.action.reason.cover_full":"Every friendly fortification within reach is full","unit_info.action.effect.cover_stow":"Hidden and protected inside, resupplied every round; can come out from the next turn","garrison.title":"Garrison - {name}","garrison.lead":"Formations inside are hidden from the enemy, cannot be attacked on their own and are resupplied at the start of every round. Where the equipment file allows it, artillery, anti-aircraft guns and staff inside still support the fortification and its neighbours. One that went in this turn can come out next turn, onto a free hex beside the fortification. If the fortification is destroyed, everything inside is lost.","garrison.launch":"Come out","garrison.launch.hint":"Press Come out, then click the hex beside the fortification to step out onto.","garrison.status.ready":"Ready to come out","garrison.status.landed":"Went in this turn - can come out next turn","garrison.empty":"The garrison is empty. A friendly land formation beside the fortification can Take cover here.","garrison.pick":"Choose a formation to come out.","garrison.blocked.deployment":"Formations come out from the first turn; during deployment you can only send one back to the reserve.","garrison.blocked.landed":"It went in this turn and can come out next turn.","garrison.blocked.no_room":"No free hex to come out onto: the hexes around are occupied.","garrison.entered":"{unit} took cover in {container}","hangar.stowed":"{unit} placed in the hangar of {container}","hangar.landed":"{unit} landed in the hangar of {container}","hangar.launch.pick_hex":"Choose the hex to come out onto","hangar.launched.fly":"Airborne - click where it flies","hangar.blocked.no_room":"No free hex to take off onto: the hexes around are occupied.","hangar.blocked.landed":"It landed this turn and can take off next turn.","hangar.blocked.deployment":"Take-offs begin with the first turn; during deployment you can only send a formation back to the reserve.","hangar.blocked.turn":"Only on your own turn.","hangar.pick":"Choose a formation to take off.","hangar.empty":"The hangar is empty. Land an aircraft here, or place one from the reserve at deployment.","hangar.reserve":"Back to reserve","hangar.launch.hint":"Take off, then click where it flies.","hangar.launch":"Take off","hangar.status.landed":"Landed this turn - ready next turn","hangar.status.ready":"Ready for take-off","hangar.ammo":"Ammo","hangar.fuel":"Fuel","hangar.not_used":"not used","hangar.free_place":"Free place","hangar.lead":"Formations inside are hidden from the enemy and take up no slot on the map. At the start of every round aircraft are refuelled, rearmed and repaired to full strength as far as your prestige allows (at half price in an Airbase). One that landed this turn can take off next turn. If this unit is destroyed, everything inside is lost.","hangar.close":"Close","hangar.count":"{used} / {max}","hangar.title":"Hangar - {name}","unit_info.action.effect.hangar_occupancy":"{amount} of {detail} places taken","unit_info.action.effect.hangar_stow":"Hidden and safe inside; refuelled, rearmed and repaired every round; can take off from the next turn","unit_info.action.reason.hangar_full":"Every friendly hangar within reach is full","unit_info.action.hangar.help":"Open this unit's hangar: see which formations are inside, their fuel and ammunition, and order one to take off. Friendly aircraft land here with Land in hangar from this hex or the six around it; at deployment, click a carrier or airbase with a reserve aircraft selected to put it straight inside.","unit_info.action.hangar.label":"Hangar","unit_info.action.hangar_land.help":"Put this formation inside the friendly carrier or airbase on or beside its hex. Inside a hangar it cannot be seen or attacked and does not take the hex's slot. At the start of every round an aircraft inside is refuelled, rearmed and repaired to full strength as far as your prestige allows - at half price in an Airbase. It can take off again from your next turn. If the carrier or airbase is destroyed, everything inside is lost with it.","unit_info.action.hangar_land.label":"Land in hangar","unit_info.action.withdraw.help":"Takes this formation off the map and back into Reserves, so it can be placed on another hex. Only during the opening deployment, before any of your formations has moved or fired. An auxiliary lent by this battle can be withdrawn too, and stays an auxiliary.","unit_info.action.effect.withdraw_to_tray":"Returns to Reserves; no prestige is spent or refunded.","unit_info.action.effect.withdraw_auxiliary_to_tray":"Returns to Reserves as an auxiliary: it can be placed again, but it does not join your core and stays behind when the battle ends.","unit_info.action.wake.help":"Returns this formation to ready-unit navigation.","unit_info.action.wake.label":"Wake","unit_info.action.disembark.label":"Disembark","unit_info.action.status.available":"Available","unit_info.action.status.unavailable":"Unavailable","unit_info.action.gain.ammo":"+{value} ammo","unit_info.action.gain.fuel":"+{value} fuel","unit_info.action.gain.strength":"+{value} strength","unit_info.action.gain.summary":"{gains} \u00b7 {context} ({efficiency}%)","unit_info.action.resupply.blocked":"Can\u2019t resupply","unit_info.action.green_reinforce.done":"+{value} strength from raw recruits (experience {from} \u2192 {to})","unit_info.action.green_reinforce.help":"Bring the formation back up to strength with raw recruits: a fraction of the usual price, paid for in experience.","unit_info.action.green_reinforce.label":"Green replacements","unit_info.action.dismiss_leader.done":"The commander has left the formation","unit_info.action.dismiss_leader.help":"Send this commander away, freeing the formation to find another later.","unit_info.action.dismiss_leader.label":"Dismiss commander","unit_info.action.reinforce.blocked":"Can\u2019t reinforce","unit_info.action.overstrength.blocked":"No overstrength","unit_info.action.reason.already_moved":"Already moved this turn.","unit_info.action.reason.already_fired":"Already fired this turn.","unit_info.action.reason.already_resupplied":"Already supplied or reinforced this turn.","unit_info.action.reason.no_organic_transport":"No organic transport assigned.","unit_info.action.reason.no_transport_available":"No transport point left in the pool.","unit_info.action.reason.not_at_transport_facility":"Not at a valid port or airfield.","unit_info.action.reason.no_disembark_hex":"No free adjacent hex to unload into.","unit_info.action.reason.fully_supplied":"Already fully supplied.","unit_info.action.reason.no_airfield":"Not on or beside an own airfield, and not on an own carrier.","unit_info.action.reason.invalid_supply_terrain":"This formation cannot be supplied here.","unit_info.action.reason.at_full_strength":"Already at full strength.","unit_info.action.reason.no_strength_restored_here":"Local supply restores no strength here.","unit_info.action.reason.needs_prestige":"Needs {amount} more prestige.","unit_info.action.reason.needs_experience":"Needs {amount} more experience.","unit_info.action.reason.overstrength_spent":"Overstrength has already been used.","unit_info.action.reason.overstrength_cap_reached":"Already at the limit its experience allows.","unit_info.action.reason.undo_new_intelligence":"The move revealed new information, so it is final.","unit_info.action.reason.undo_surprised":"The formation was caught by surprise, so the move is final.","unit_info.action.reason.undo_intercepted":"Anti-air fire intercepted the move, so it is final.","unit_info.action.reason.undo_combat":"Combat made this move final.","unit_info.action.reason.undo_irreversible_action":"A later irreversible command made this move final.","unit_info.action.reason.undo_nothing_to_undo":"There is no recorded move to undo.","unit_info.action.reason.no_action_left":"Nothing left for this formation to do this turn.","unit_info.action.reason.not_local_turn":"Commands cannot be issued right now.","unit_info.action.effect.mount_transport_stats":"The transport\u2019s movement and vulnerability apply.","unit_info.action.effect.dismount_own_stats":"The formation\u2019s own combat and movement statistics apply.","unit_info.action.effect.limber_toggle_free":"Limbering is free, but does not return a move already spent.","unit_info.action.effect.embark_air":"Carried by air transport; it cannot fight normally while carried.","unit_info.action.effect.embark_drops_transport":"Its organic transport cannot fly and is left behind for good.","unit_info.action.effect.embark_naval":"Carried by naval transport; it cannot fight normally while carried.","unit_info.action.effect.disembark":"Unloads onto one of {amount} adjacent hexes.","unit_info.action.effect.supply_ammo":"+{amount} ammunition","unit_info.action.effect.supply_fuel":"+{amount} fuel","unit_info.action.effect.supply_transport_ammo":"+{amount} transport ammunition","unit_info.action.effect.supply_transport_fuel":"+{amount} transport fuel","unit_info.action.effect.supply_efficiency":"{amount}% local supply efficiency","unit_info.action.effect.strength_gain":"+{amount} strength","unit_info.action.effect.prestige_cost":"{amount} prestige","unit_info.action.effect.prestige_cost_once":"{amount} prestige","unit_info.action.effect.engineering_start_after_move":"May begin after moving, if the formation has not fired or resupplied this turn","unit_info.action.effect.engineering_start_unspent":"Must begin before the formation moves, fires or resupplies this turn","unit_info.action.effect.overstrength_target":"Strength {amount}, out of a limit of {detail}","unit_info.action.effect.ends_unit_action":"Uses this formation\u2019s action for the turn.","unit_info.action.effect.undo_restore":"Restores the previous position, fuel and movement state.","unit_info.action.effect.sleep_skip":"Skipped in ready-unit navigation; the end-turn warning still counts it.","unit_info.action.effect.wake_restore":"Returns to ready-unit navigation if it can still act.","unit_info.carrier.help":"Carrier \u2014 click to view.","unit_info.entrenchment.value":"Entrenchment: {value}","unit_info.entrenchment.cannot_dig":"This class does not dig in: its level comes from the scenario and only goes down.","unit_info.entrenchment.terrain":"Terrain \u201c{terrain}\u201d: base level {base}.","unit_info.entrenchment.crater":"A shell crater raises the base level here to {value}.","unit_info.entrenchment.attachment":"Attachment: +{value} to the base level.","unit_info.entrenchment.growth":"A formation that stays put gets the base level {base} at once when the next turn begins, then digs in further slowly (faster with experience), up to {max}.","unit_info.entrenchment.loss":"Moving resets entrenchment to 0. Each hit takes 1 level, a barrage takes 2.","unit_info.entrenchment.compare":"Base levels under these rules: city {city}, forest {forest}, fortification {fortification}.","unit_info.entrenchment.combat":"In combat: +{value} to defence. This is added to the stat, not a percentage cut in losses.","unit_info.entrenchment.doubled":"Infantry attacked by a vehicle in a city, forest, mountains or a fortification counts it twice: +{value}.","unit_info.entrenchment.rugged":"Base chance of a rugged defence: {value}% (5% per level). Only against an infantry attack from an adjacent hex, and only while this unit has ammunition; a surprise attack never raises one, and an attacker that ignores entrenchment, or has Infiltration Tactics, or Street Fighter in a city or port, avoids it. Tenacious Defence commanders change the chance.","unit_info.entrenchment.rugged.against.none":"Against {unit}: no rugged defence. It needs an infantry attack from an adjacent hex, ammunition on this side, and an attacker that does not avoid it.","unit_info.entrenchment.rugged.against":"Against {unit}: {value}% chance of a rugged defence.","unit_info.entrenchment.rugged.no_ammo":"No ammunition now: no rugged defence until it is resupplied.","unit_info.entrenchment.against":"Against {unit}: +{value} to defence.","unit_info.entrenchment.against.doubled":"Against {unit}: +{value} to defence (counted twice).","unit_info.entrenchment.against.bypassed":"{unit} ignores this entrenchment: +0 to defence.","unit_info.entrenchment.weather":"Weather and ground condition do not change the entrenchment level.","unit_info.entrenchment.precipitation":"Rain or snow now: both sides get a further +{value} to defence, separate from entrenchment (not in rugged combat).","unit_info.collapse.help":"Fold the unit card away so it stops covering the map. Bring it back with the button in the map\u2019s bottom-left corner.","unit_info.expand.help":"Show the unit card again.","unit_info.experience.value":"Experience: {experience}/{max}","unit_info.experience.value_with_support":"Experience: {experience}/{max}. Combat Support adds {bars} effective bar(s).","unit_info.formation.commander.label":"Heroic commander","unit_info.formation.destroyed.label":"Enemy formations destroyed","unit_info.formation.honours.label":"Battle honours","unit_info.formation.objectives.label":"Objectives captured","unit_info.formation.recognition.label":"Recognition","unit_info.formation.scenarios.label":"Scenarios recorded","unit_info.formation.service_record.aria":"Open service record for {formation}","unit_info.formation.service_record.help":"Open the complete chronological formation history.","unit_info.formation.service_record.label":"SERVICE RECORD","unit_info.formation.summary":"{label}: {value}","unit_info.grounded.help":"Grounded \u2014 bad weather prevents air units from attacking this turn.","unit_info.group.attack.help":"Attack values used against each enemy target type; higher is better.","unit_info.group.attack.label":"Attack","unit_info.group.defence.help":"Defensive values used for different attacks and ranges; higher is better.","unit_info.group.defence.label":"Defence","unit_info.group.mobility_recon.help":"Movement, firing range, initiative and battlefield detection.","unit_info.group.mobility_recon.label":"Mobility & Recon","unit_info.group.status.help":"Current unit resources and battlefield condition.","unit_info.group.status.label":"Status","unit_info.identity.class_service":"{class} \u00b7 {service}","unit_info.identity.service.core":"CORE","unit_info.identity.service.core.full":"core unit","unit_info.identity.service.core.help":"A permanent unit of your army: it stays with you for the whole campaign. If it survives, it carries into the next battle with its experience, honours and commander. If it is destroyed, it is gone for good.","unit_info.identity.service.auxiliary":"AUX","unit_info.identity.service.auxiliary.full":"auxiliary unit","unit_info.identity.service.auxiliary.help":"Attached to you for this battle only. It leaves afterwards, taking its experience with it, and disbanding it refunds no prestige. It need not be spared the way core units are.","unit_info.identity.service.scenario":"SCENARIO","unit_info.identity.service.scenario.full":"scenario unit","unit_info.identity.service.scenario.help":"Fights in this scenario only and does not carry into a campaign.","unit_info.identity.capture.yes":"Can capture towns, flags and objectives.","unit_info.identity.capture.no":"Cannot capture towns or objectives \u2014 that takes infantry or armour.","unit_info.identity.role.infantry":"Infantry: holds hard in towns, forests and mountains and entrenches well. Vulnerable to tanks in the open.","unit_info.identity.role.tank":"Tanks: fast armoured striking power, strong against vehicles and infantry in the open. Beware infantry in towns and forests.","unit_info.identity.role.recon":"Recon: fast and far-sighted, uncovers enemy positions. Weak in a real fight.","unit_info.identity.role.anti_tank":"Anti-tank guns: strong against armour, especially on defence. Vulnerable to infantry and on the march.","unit_info.identity.role.flak":"Flak: shoots down aircraft and covers neighbouring units against them; can also fire at ground targets.","unit_info.identity.role.fortification":"Fortification: immobile, but holds a key position stubbornly.","unit_info.identity.role.ground_transport":"Ground transport: carries infantry and guns. Nearly defenceless in combat.","unit_info.identity.role.artillery":"Artillery: strikes from range without return fire and supports neighbouring units on defence. Vulnerable up close.","unit_info.identity.role.air_defence":"Air defence: long-range anti-aircraft cover for the area.","unit_info.identity.role.fighter":"Fighters: win the sky \u2014 shoot down enemy aircraft and escort your bombers.","unit_info.identity.role.tactical_bomber":"Tactical bombers: strike ground targets. Need cover from fighters and flak.","unit_info.identity.role.level_bomber":"Level bombers: heavy strikes on ground targets from altitude. Vulnerable to fighters.","unit_info.identity.role.air_transport":"Air transport: ferries infantry and paratroopers. Defenceless in combat.","unit_info.identity.role.submarine":"Submarine: attacks ships from hiding and is hard to detect.","unit_info.identity.role.destroyer":"Destroyer: a fast submarine hunter and escort for larger ships.","unit_info.identity.role.battleship":"Battleship: heavy guns engage ships and the coast at long range.","unit_info.identity.role.carrier":"Carrier: a floating airfield for your aircraft.","unit_info.identity.role.airbase":"Airbase: immobile ground service for aircraft, not the airfield itself.","unit_info.identity.role.naval_transport":"Naval transport: carries troops by sea. Defenceless in combat.","unit_info.identity.role.battle_cruiser":"Battlecruiser: fast with heavy guns, but less protected than a battleship.","unit_info.identity.role.cruiser":"Cruiser: an all-round ship for surface fights and shore bombardment.","unit_info.identity.role.light_cruiser":"Light cruiser: fast ship for fighting light forces and escort duty.","unit_info.leader.authored_commander":"authored heroic leader","unit_info.leader.candidate.help":"No hero has emerged in this formation\nRecognition: {recognition}\n{chanceLine}\nDrought protection: {drought}/{guaranteedAfter}","unit_info.leader.candidate.label":"Hero yet to emerge","unit_info.leader.candidate.no_record":"No hero has emerged in this formation. It has no recognition record yet.","unit_info.leader.eligibility.help":"In campaigns, your permanent core units can gain heroic commanders. Auxiliary and scenario-only units cannot gain a persistent hero.","unit_info.leader.chance":"Next notable action: {chance}% hero emergence chance","unit_info.leader.checks_unlock":"Hero emergence checks unlock at {target} recognition","unit_info.leader.guaranteed":"Next notable action: hero emergence guaranteed","unit_info.leader.hero.short":"{rank} {name}","unit_info.leader.led_by":"Heroic commander: {rank} {name}","unit_info.leader.legacy":"Experienced Leader: {trait}","unit_info.leader.open_dossier.aria":"{label}. Open commander dossier","unit_info.leader.open_dossier.help":"Click to open the commander dossier.","unit_info.leader.scenario_only.help":"Scenario-only formation: persistent hero development is unavailable.","unit_info.leader.scenario_only.label":"No persistent hero","unit_info.leader.temporary.help":"This formation is explicitly temporary and does not develop a persistent hero.","unit_info.leader.temporary.label":"Temporary auxiliary formation","unit_info.stat.uAAir.help":"Air attack: attack power against aircraft.","unit_info.stat.uAHard.help":"Hard attack: attack power against tanks and other armoured targets.","unit_info.stat.uANaval.help":"Naval attack: attack power against ships and landing craft.","unit_info.stat.uASoft.help":"Soft attack: attack power against infantry, artillery and unarmoured targets.","unit_info.stat.uAmmo.help":"Ammo: attacks and defensive fire consume it. A unit with no ammo cannot fire; resupply restores it.","unit_info.stat.uDAir.help":"Air defence: protection when attacked by an aircraft.","unit_info.stat.uDClose.help":"Close defence: protection in adjacent close combat.","unit_info.stat.uDHard.help":"Ground defence: protection when attacked by a ground unit.","unit_info.stat.uDRange.help":"Ranged defence modifier: extra protection against ground fire from outside close-combat range.","unit_info.stat.uEnt.help":"Entrenchment: defensive preparation gained by holding position. Moving usually removes it.","unit_info.stat.uExp.help":"Experience: earned in combat. Higher experience improves combat performance and carries over with core units.","unit_info.stat.uFuel.help":"Fuel: spent while moving. At zero, fuel-using units cannot move; resupply restores it.","unit_info.stat.uGunRange.help":"Firing range in hexes. A value of 1 means the target must be adjacent.","unit_info.stat.uIni.help":"Initiative: higher initiative usually fires first, reducing the enemy\u2019s return fire.","unit_info.stat.uMoveType.help":"Movement type: determines terrain costs and whether roads, rails or special transport are required.","unit_info.stat.uMovement.help":"Movement points available each turn; terrain and enemy zones of control change their cost.","unit_info.stat.uSpot.help":"Spotting range: maximum distance at which this unit can reveal terrain and hidden enemies.","unit_info.stat.uStr.help":"Strength: remaining soldiers or vehicles. Damage reduces combat effectiveness; reinforce to restore it.","unit_info.stat.uTarget.help":"Target type: soft, hard, air or naval; determines which enemy attack value is used against this unit.","unit_info.state.help":"Current temporary battlefield state.","unit_info.state.mounted.help":"MOUNTED: the formation is currently using its organic transport.","unit_info.state.mounted.label":"MOUNTED","unit_info.state.reserve.help":"RESERVE: the formation is waiting to be deployed.","unit_info.state.reserve.label":"RESERVE","unit_info.state.suppressed.h